[32m+[m[32m# The gallery[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```sh[m
[32m+[m[32mzig build gallery                 # render and diff against the references[m
[32m+[m[32mzig build gallery -- --update     # accept the current renders[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe arbiter for the [experience roadmap](roadmap/experience.md), the way[m
[32m+[m[32m`zig build bench` is for the [performance](roadmap/performance.md) one. The[m
[32m+[m[32mperformance rule is that a claim carries a number or it is a guess; nothing[m
[32m+[m[32mabove the renderer has a number, so visual work is judged by pictures[m
[32m+[m[32minstead.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mTen captures render one canonical screen each through the real parser, grid[m
[32m+[m[32mand renderer, and are compared pixel by pixel against a committed PNG.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## What it measures[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mPer capture: the rendered size, how many pixels differ from the reference,[m
[32m+[m[32mand the worst single-channel delta.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32m  capture                       size    differing     worst  result[m
[32m+[m[32m  ---------------------- ----------- ------------ ---------  ----------------[m
[32m+[m[32m  typography-14pt-1x         678x199            0         0  identical[m
[32m+[m[32m  cursor-14pt-1x              444x80           17       194  0.05% of pixels[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m`worst` separates the two kinds of change that matter. A handful of pixels[m
[32m+[m[32mat a large delta is a shape moving — a glyph, a rule, the cursor. Many[m
[32m+[m[32mpixels at a delta of 1 or 2 is a colour or blending change. The example[m
[32m+[m[32mabove is the cursor drawn one pixel narrower.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**It never fails the build.** Like the bench, it reports and CI posts the[m
[32m+[m[32mresult; a diff is usually an intended visual change and the reviewer is the[m
[32m+[m[32mone who decides. Renders land in `bench/gallery/current/`, which is not[m
[32m+[m[32mcommitted.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## How it runs headless[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m`SDL_VIDEODRIVER=dummy` — put into the child's environment by `gallery.zig`[m
[32m+[m[32mitself — gives SDL a video backend with no display, and `--screenshot` reads[m
[32m+[m[32mthe frame back through `SDL_RenderReadPixels` *before* present. So a capture is exactly what the[m
[32m+[m[32mrenderer produced, needs no screen-recording permission, and works on a CI[m
[32m+[m[32mrunner. (The `offscreen` driver does not work; it fails to create a window.)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m`--scale N` tells the app to pretend the display has that pixel density[m
[32m+[m[32mrather than asking it. That is the only way a 2× capture is reproducible on[m
[32m+[m[32ma 1× machine, and it is why the gallery can assert Retina rendering from CI.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mCaptures are cropped to the grid's own pixel size. A window's size is set in[m
[32m+[m[32mlogical units, so on a 2× display an odd pixel height rounds up by one and[m
[32m+[m[32mthe same capture would differ by a row depending on the machine that took[m
[32m+[m[32mit. A reference has to be reproducible anywhere or it is not a reference.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mPNGs are written by `src/png.zig`, about a hundred lines over[m
[32m+[m[32m`std.compress.flate` — 8-bit RGBA, no interlacing, filter 0. The project[m
[32m+[m[32mlinks libc and the system's own frameworks and nothing else[m
[32m+[m[32m([dependencies.md](roadmap/dependencies.md)), and a picture format is not a[m
[32m+[m[32mgood reason to break that.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## The scenes[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m`bench/gallery/*.sh`, each printing a fixed byte stream:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| scene | what it covers |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|[m
[32m+[m[32m| `typography` | printable ASCII, descenders and ascenders, box drawing, blocks, braille, CJK, emoji |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `attributes` | every SGR attribute, alone and combined |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `colors` | the 16 ANSI slots, the 256-colour cube, a truecolour ramp |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `tui` | a scroll region, a framed panel and a status line — the shape an agent TUI draws |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `cursor` | the cursor, in a scene whose only interesting feature is the cursor |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m`typography` is captured at 10, 14 and 20 pt, and at 1× and 2×, because[m
[32m+[m[32mbaseline placement and cell rounding are what change between sizes.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**The scenes are scripts, not programs.** Not `vim`, not `htop`: their[m
[32m+[m[32moutput varies with version, terminal size, locale and whatever files are[m
[32m+[m[32mlying around, and a pixel diff cannot tell that apart from a regression.[m
[32m+[m[32mThe bench corpora are committed files for the same reason. Real-program[m
[32m+[m[32mscreens want recorded byte streams, which is what[m
[32m+[m[32m[A0](roadmap/agentic.md) will produce.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Adding a scene[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mWrite `bench/gallery/<name>.sh` so that it prints and exits — the capture is[m
[32m+[m[32mtaken from the final frame, so nothing needs to sleep. Add a row to[m
[32m+[m[32m`captures` in `src/gallery.zig`, run `zig build gallery -- --update`, and[m
[32m+[m[32mcommit the PNG along with the change that made it necessary.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mKeep captures small. They are committed and they stay in the history: the[m
[32m+[m[32mten here are 152 KB in total.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## When the references need regenerating[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAny intended visual change. Run with `--update`, look at every image that[m
[32m+[m[32mmoved, and say in the PR why each one did. An `--update` that nobody looked[m
[32m+[m[32mat is worse than no gallery, because it launders a regression into the[m
[32m+[m[32mreference.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe references are rendered on a maintainer's Mac. A CI runner whose system[m
[32m+[m[32mfont differs by a version shows a delta that is not a regression — read the[m
[32m+[m[32muploaded renders rather than the percentages.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mHow large a delta: on the first CI run every capture's *size* matched, the[m
[32m+[m[32m`colors` scene (rectangles, no glyphs) was byte-identical, and the nine[m
[32m+[m[32mscenes containing text differed by 1.1–2.6% of pixels. So the cross-machine[m
[32m+[m[32mdifference is entirely glyph rasterization, and nothing else in the[m
[32m+[m[32mrenderer. [D1](roadmap/dependencies.md) should take those nine to zero.[m
[1mdiff --git a/docs/roadmap/completed/sprint-x0-gallery.md b/docs/roadmap/completed/sprint-x0-gallery.md[m
[1mnew file mode 100644[m
[1mindex 0000000..cbc0650[m
[1m--- /dev/null[m
[1m+++ b/docs/roadmap/completed/sprint-x0-gallery.md[m
[36m@@ -0,0 +1,163 @@[m
[32m+[m[32m# Sprint X0 — The gallery[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Done.** First sprint on the [experience roadmap](../experience.md), and[m
[32m+[m[32mrow 1 of the [priorities](../priorities.md) order.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## What was proposed[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mTurn `--screenshot` into an acceptance test: scripts under `bench/gallery/`[m
[32m+[m[32meach rendering one canonical screen, captured at 1× and 2×, committed as[m
[32m+[m[32mPNGs, with `zig build gallery` re-rendering and reporting per-image pixel[m
[32m+[m[32mdeltas and CI posting them non-gating.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mRisk was called **low** — "the flag exists; this is scripting around it".[m
[32m+[m[32mThat was wrong in an interesting way, and the two things it missed are the[m
[32m+[m[32msprint.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## What it actually needed[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Rendering with no display.** `--screenshot` existed but nothing had ever[m
[32m+[m[32mrun the app without a window. `SDL_VIDEODRIVER=dummy` gives SDL a backend[m
[32m+[m[32mwith no display and `SDL_RenderReadPixels` still returns a correct frame, so[m
[32m+[m[32ma capture works on a CI runner. The `offscreen` driver, which sounds like[m
[32m+[m[32mthe right one, fails to create a window at all.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**A pixel density that does not depend on the machine.** A 2× capture was[m
[32m+[m[32mimpossible on a 1× runner, because the renderer asked the display how dense[m
[32m+[m[32mit was. `--scale N` tells it to pretend instead, and `Renderer.init` now[m
[32m+[m[32msizes the window so its *pixel* size fits the grid at that scale — without[m
[32m+[m[32mthat, forcing 2× rendered double-size glyphs into a single-size window and[m
[32m+[m[32mshowed half the columns.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**A PNG codec.** The flag wrote BMP via SDL, and 152 KB of committed[m
[32m+[m[32mcaptures would have been about a megabyte. `src/png.zig` is roughly a[m
[32m+[m[32mhundred lines over `std.compress.flate` — 8-bit RGBA, no interlacing, filter[m
[32m+[m[32m0, encode and decode. The project links libc and the system's own frameworks[m
[32m+[m[32mand nothing else ([dependencies.md](../dependencies.md)); a picture format is[m
[32m+[m[32mnot a good reason to break that. Its own tests found the first bug: the[m
[32m+[m[32mdecoder accepted a file with no `IEND` chunk, so a truncated capture came[m
[32m+[m[32mback as a shorter picture rather than an error.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Two bugs found by building it[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**The app could lose the tail of a program's output.** The event loop ends[m
[32m+[m[32mwhen `pty.exited()` notices the child is gone, which can happen while bytes[m
[32m+[m[32mit already wrote are still in the PTY buffer. Interactively you would never[m
[32m+[m[32msee it; a gallery scene that prints and exits in milliseconds hits it every[m
[32m+[m[32mtime. The exit path now stops the reader, joins it, and drains what is left[m
[32m+[m[32mbefore the final frame.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**`--screenshot` could not capture a short-lived program at all.** It fired[m
[32m+[m[32mone second in, and every scene here is gone before that. The last frame is[m
[32m+[m[32mnow captured on the way out if the timer never fired, which also makes the[m
[32m+[m[32mcapture deterministic rather than "whatever was on screen at one second".[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## The captures[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mTen, 152 KB in total:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| scene | what it covers |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|[m
[32m+[m[32m| `typography` | printable ASCII, descenders, box drawing, blocks, braille, CJK, emoji |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `attributes` | every SGR attribute, alone and combined |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `colors` | 16 ANSI slots, the 256-colour cube, a truecolour ramp |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `tui` | a scroll region, a framed panel, a status line |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `cursor` | a scene whose only interesting feature is the cursor |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m`typography` at 10, 14 and 20 pt and at 1× and 2×, because baseline[m
[32m+[m[32mplacement and cell rounding are what change between sizes.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe scenes are scripts printing fixed bytes, **not `vim` and `htop`** as the[m
[32m+[m[32msprint text suggested. Their output varies with version, terminal size,[m
[32m+[m[32mlocale and the files lying around, and a pixel diff cannot tell that apart[m
[32m+[m[32mfrom a regression — the bench corpora are committed files for exactly this[m
[32m+[m[32mreason. Real-program screens want recorded byte streams, which[m
[32m+[m[32m[A0](../agentic.md) produces.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Done when[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m> the gallery runs headless on the macOS CI runner and a one-pixel change in[m
[32m+[m[32m> the cursor shows up as a diff in the PR summary[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mBoth. Headless locally and as a CI job that uploads the renders and writes[m
[32m+[m[32mthe table to the job summary. The cursor condition was demonstrated by[m
[32m+[m[32mbreaking it two ways:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| mutation | 1× | 2× | worst delta |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|---|---|[m
[32m+[m[32m| cursor block one pixel narrower | 17 pixels | 34 pixels | 194 |[m
[32m+[m[32m| cursor colour +1 in one channel | 153 pixels | 578 pixels | 1 |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe `worst` column is what separates the two: a few pixels at a large delta[m
[32m+[m[32mis a shape moving, many pixels at a delta of 1 is a colour change.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## What the first gallery shows[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe typography page has **empty cells** where braille, CJK and emoji should[m
[32m+[m[32mbe, and the box-drawing row is partial. That is not a regression; it is the[m
[32m+[m[32m"missing glyphs are drawn as nothing" row of the experience roadmap's[m
[32m+[m[32mwhere-we-are table, which until now was a sentence. It is [X2](../experience.md)'s[m
[32m+[m[32mjob, and the gallery is how anyone will be able to tell it worked.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## What review found[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFive defects, all fixed before merge. Two of them mattered enough to change[m
[32m+[m[32mwhat the sprint means.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**The gallery was not headless.** `std.process.spawn` with no environment[m
[32m+[m[32mmap hands the child an *empty* environment, so the `SDL_VIDEODRIVER=dummy`[m
[32m+[m[32mthe build step set never reached the app. Every reference in the first draft[m
[32m+[m[32mwas rendered through the real Cocoa and Metal backend at the maintainer's[m
[32m+[m[32mdisplay density, while the documentation, the build comment and the CI job[m
[32m+[m[32mall said otherwise. Running it genuinely headless made all ten fail — five[m
[32m+[m[32mof them on size alone, which skips the pixel diff entirely, so the arbiter[m
[32m+[m[32mwould have been blind for half its captures. `gallery.zig` now builds the[m
[32m+[m[32mchild's environment itself, which also means `zig build gallery` is headless[m
[32m+[m[32mhowever it was invoked.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**A capture depended on the machine that took it.** The window size is set[m
[32m+[m[32min logical units, so `want_px / density` rounds: on a 2× display an odd[m
[32m+[m[32mpixel height became an even one, and the same capture differed by a row[m
[32m+[m[32mbetween machines — the exact dependency `--scale` exists to remove.[m
[32m+[m[32mScreenshots are now cropped to the grid's own pixel size.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mAlso fixed: `png.decode` multiplied header fields in `u32` before bounding[m
[32m+[m[32mthem, so a 70-byte file claiming 0x40000000 × 1 panicked in a safe build and[m
[32m+[m[32mreturned a bogus image in a fast one; and one unreadable reference aborted[m
[32m+[m[32mthe whole run rather than reporting that capture and continuing.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**And a regression this sprint introduced.** The drain added above waited[m
[32m+[m[32mfor the PTY to go quiet — which a live child never allows. Closing the[m
[32m+[m[32mwindow while a command was producing output hung the app until it was[m
[32m+[m[32mkilled. The drain now runs only when the child has actually exited, and[m
[32m+[m[32munder a deadline.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## What the first CI run measured[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe gallery's first run on the macOS runner is more useful than a pass:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| | |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|[m
[32m+[m[32m| every capture's **size** | matches exactly |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `colors-14pt-1x` | **identical, 0 pixels** |[m
[32m+[m[32m| the nine scenes containing text | differ by 1.1–2.6% of pixels, worst delta 19–97 |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m`colors` is the only scene made entirely of background rectangles and no[m
[32m+[m[32mglyphs. It matching byte for byte, while every scene with text differs, puts[m
[32m+[m[32ma number on something that was previously a caveat: **the whole difference[m
[32m+[m[32mbetween this machine and the runner is glyph rasterization.** Geometry,[m
[32m+[m[32mlayout, colour, blending and the vertex path are identical across machines.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThat is also the argument for [D1](../dependencies.md), owning the[m
[32m+[m[32mrasterizer, stated as a measurement rather than a preference: FreeType[m
[32m+[m[32magainst a system font whose version moves is the only thing standing between[m
[32m+[m[32mthis gallery and an exact cross-machine reference. When D1 lands, these nine[m
[32m+[m[32mshould go to zero, and that is a testable prediction rather than a hope.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Not gating, deliberately[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mLike the bench. A visual diff is usually an intended change and the reviewer[m
[32m+[m[32mdecides. The references are also rendered on a maintainer's Mac, so a runner[m
[32m+[m[32mwith a different system font version reads as a whole-image delta that is[m
[32m+[m[32mnot a regression — the job says so, and uploads the renders so a person can[m
[32m+[m[32mlook rather than trust a percentage.[m
