[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- The screen is a row ring, so a line feed rotates an offset instead of[m
[32m+[m[32m  moving the grid — 1.7–3.8× on every corpus containing a newline.[m
[32m+[m[32m- The wait for vblank moved out of the terminal mutex. Bulk output through a[m
[32m+[m[32m  real PTY went from 0.26–0.40 MiB/s to 41–51 MiB/s, and the lock is held[m
[32m+[m[32m  2 µs per frame rather than roughly 8 ms.[m
[32m+[m[32m- The frame is one `SDL_RenderGeometryRaw` call rather than 850–2,350 SDL[m
[32m+[m[32m  calls, which took the worst-case frame build from 8–9 ms to about 0.2 ms.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Runs of printable ASCII reach the terminal as one slice: the `ascii`[m
[32m+[m[32m  corpus went from 111 to 481 MiB/s, and end-to-end throughput to 66 MiB/s.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mTwo planned sprints were retired by their own gates without being built:[m
[32m+[m[32mshrinking the cell to 8 bytes, and per-row damage tracking.[m
 [m
