 | wheel | scroll history, or arrow keys on the alternate screen |[m
 [m
[31m-Flags: `--font-size N`, `--size COLSxROWS`, `--shell PATH`, `--frame-stats`[m
[31m-(frame timing to stderr, once a second), `--screenshot PATH` (save the frame[m
[31m-drawn one second in, as a BMP).[m
[32m+[m[32mFlags: `--font-size N` (6–72), `--size COLSxROWS` (up to 1000 each),[m
[32m+[m[32m`--shell PATH`, `--frame-stats` (frame timing to stderr, once a second),[m
[32m+[m[32m`--screenshot PATH` (save the frame drawn one second in, as a BMP).[m
 [m
 ## How it fits together[m
 [m
[36m@@ -57,6 +57,7 @@[m [mPTY ──► vt.Parser ──► Terminal ──► Renderer ──► SDL3 ─[m
 | `theme.zig` | 16 ANSI colors plus the generated xterm cube and grayscale ramp. |[m
 | `main.zig` | Reader thread, event loop, the mutex between them. |[m
 | `stats.zig` | The `--frame-stats` timer: lock hold, build and present per frame. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| `cli.zig` | Command-line options, and the bounds on anything the renderer will size a window from. |[m
 [m
 Two threads: one reads the PTY and feeds the parser, the main thread draws.[m
 One mutex between them, held by the main thread only long enough to copy the[m
[1mdiff --git a/docs/roadmap/completed/sprint-1-vsync-lock.md b/docs/roadmap/completed/sprint-1-vsync-lock.md[m
[1mindex adfab7d..c5900d2 100644[m
[1m--- a/docs/roadmap/completed/sprint-1-vsync-lock.md[m
[1m+++ b/docs/roadmap/completed/sprint-1-vsync-lock.md[m
[36m@@ -90,6 +90,21 @@[m [mmeans [Sprint 4](../performance.md) — the printable-run fast path — will[m
 show up directly in this measurement, not only in the headless bench. That[m
 is the attribution the roadmap said this sprint had to make possible.[m
 [m
[32m+[m[32m## Follow-up: a defect this record did not catch[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mCode review of the merged sprints found that `main.zig` clears `term.dirty`[m
[32m+[m[32m*before* attempting the snapshot, so when the snapshot's allocation fails[m
[32m+[m[32mthe `catch` skips the frame and nothing sets the flag again — on an idle[m
[32m+[m[32mterminal the child's last line would stay invisible until the user typed.[m
[32m+[m[32mThe doc comment written here for `snapshot` ("a redraw can be skipped but[m
[32m+[m[32mnever drawn from a half-copied grid") was therefore too generous to itself:[m
[32m+[m[32mskipping was permanent, not per-iteration. Fixed by restoring `dirty` inside[m
[32m+[m[32mthe `catch`, still under the lock.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m`snapshot` itself was correct on that path — it allocates before freeing and[m
[32m+[m[32massigns `cols`/`rows` only after the `try` — so there was never a dangling[m
[32m+[m[32mbuffer or a half-copied frame.[m
[32m+[m
 ## What the timer sees that the bench does not[m
 [m
 The `build` column occasionally spikes to ~8 ms in the first second of a run[m
[1mdiff --git a/docs/roadmap/completed/sprint-2-one-draw-call.md b/docs/roadmap/completed/sprint-2-one-draw-call.md[m
[1mindex 0ae695e..97101c9 100644[m
[1m--- a/docs/roadmap/completed/sprint-2-one-draw-call.md[m
[1m+++ b/docs/roadmap/completed/sprint-2-one-draw-call.md[m
[36m@@ -90,6 +90,29 @@[m [mCJK and emoji cells come out blank — SF Mono has no glyphs for them and[m
 there is no fallback face. That predates this sprint, is unchanged by it,[m
 and is a feature gap rather than a render bug.[m
 [m
[32m+[m[32m## Follow-up: two defects in the instrumentation, not the optimization[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mCode review of the merged sprints found both of this sprint's additions[m
[32m+[m[32mbroken in ways the sprint's own testing would not have found, because the[m
[32m+[m[32mmeasuring apparatus was held to a lower standard than the code it measures.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe `calls` column added to `--frame-stats` divided by the frame count with[m
[32m+[m[32mno zero guard, while `avgUs` beside it had one. A reporting window can[m
[32m+[m[32melapse with no frame drawn at all — a mouse move over an idle window wakes[m
[32m+[m[32mthe event loop without dirtying the screen — and the second such window[m
[32m+[m[32mpanics. It aborts in Debug and ReleaseSafe; on aarch64 ReleaseFast it[m
[32m+[m[32msilently yields zero, and on x86_64 it raises `SIGFPE`.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m`--size` passed its argument to `Renderer.init` unchecked, where[m
[32m+[m[32m`init_cols * cell_w + pad * 2` overflowed: `--size 4000000000x30` panicked[m
[32m+[m[32mbefore drawing anything.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mBoth are fixed, and option parsing moved to a pure `cli.zig` so the bounds[m
[32m+[m[32mhave tests — `main.zig` cannot be unit-tested because it pulls in SDL, which[m
[32m+[m[32mis exactly how an unchecked flag reached the renderer. The lesson worth[m
[32m+[m[32mkeeping: instrumentation that every claim in these records rests on deserves[m
[32m+[m[32mthe same tests as the code it measures.[m
[32m+[m
 ## What this changes about Sprint 3[m
 [m
 Sprint 3's value was already rescoped to "draw-call submission, not grid[m
[1mdiff --git a/src/cli.zig b/src/cli.zig[m
[1mnew file mode 100644[m
[1mindex 0000000..aec5bff[m
[1m--- /dev/null[m
[1m+++ b/src/cli.zig[m
[36m@@ -0,0 +1,186 @@[m
[32m+[m[32m//! Command-line options.[m
[32m+[m[32m//![m
[32m+[m[32m//! Pure: this file imports nothing but `std`, which is the point of it[m
[32m+[m[32m//! existing. `main.zig` pulls in the renderer and therefore SDL, so it has[m
[32m+[m[32m//! no place in the unit-test root -- and an unchecked `--size` accordingly[m
[32m+[m[32m//! reached `Renderer.init` and overflowed the window width. Anything that[m
[32m+[m[32m//! turns an argument into a number the renderer will use belongs here,[m
[32m+[m[32m//! where it can be tested without a window.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mconst std = @import("std");[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mpub const default_font_size = 14;[m
[32m+[m[32mpub const default_cols = 100;[m
[32m+[m[32mpub const default_rows = 30;[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m/// Bounds on every argument that reaches the renderer as a dimension.[m
[32m+[m[32m///[m
[32m+[m[32m/// The font range is the one `Cmd +`/`Cmd -` already enforces, so the flag[m
[32m+[m[32m/// cannot ask for a size the keyboard refuses. The grid bound keeps[m
[32m+[m[32m/// `cols * cell_w + padding` inside an `i32` for any font size in that[m
[32m+[m[32m/// range, which is the multiplication that overflowed.[m
[32m+[m[32mpub const min_font_size = 6;[m
[32m+[m[32mpub const max_font_size = 72;[m
[32m+[m[32mpub const max_dim = 1000;[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mpub const Options = struct {[m
[32m+[m[32m    font_size: u32 = default_font_size,[m
[32m+[m[32m    shell: ?[:0]const u8 = null,[m
[32m+[m[32m    frame_stats: bool = false,[m
[32m+[m[32m    screenshot: ?[:0]const u8 = null,[m
[32m+[m[32m    cols: u32 = default_cols,[m
[32m+[m[32m    rows: u32 = default_rows,[m
[32m+[m[32m};[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mpub const Size = struct { cols: u32, rows: u32 };[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mfn clampDim(n: u32) u32 {[m
[32m+[m[32m    return std.math.clamp(n, 1, max_dim);[m
[32m+[m[32m}[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m/// `"COLSxROWS"` as a clamped pair, or null when it is not that shape.[m
[32m+[m[32m///[m
[32m+[m[32m/// A malformed spec leaves *both* defaults alone rather than applying the[m
[32m+[m[32m/// half it could read: `--size 80xwide` meaning "80 columns and whatever[m
[32m+[m[32m/// number of rows you like" would be a worse guess than declining.[m
[32m+[m[32mpub fn parseSize(spec: []const u8) ?Size {[m
[32m+[m[32m    const x = std.mem.indexOfScalar(u8, spec, 'x') orelse return null;[m
[32m+[m[32m    const cols = std.fmt.parseInt(u32, spec[0..x], 10) catch return null;[m
[32m+[m[32m    const rows = std.fmt.parseInt(u32, spec[x + 1 ..], 10) catch return null;[m
[32m+[m[32m    return .{ .cols = clampDim(cols), .rows = clampDim(rows) };[m
[32m+[m[32m}[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mpub fn parseFontSize(spec: []const u8) ?u32 {[m
[32m+[m[32m    const n = std.fmt.parseInt(u32, spec, 10) catch return null;[m
[32m+[m[32m    return std.math.clamp(n, min_font_size, max_font_size);[m
[32m+[m[32m}[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mpub const help =[m
[32m+[m[32m    \\terminator -- a terminal emulator[m
[32m+[m[32m    \\[m
[32m+[m[32m    \\  --font-size N   point size, {d}-{d} (default {d})[m
[32m+[m[32m    \\  --size CxR      initial grid, e.g. 200x60 (default {d}x{d}, max {d})[m
[32m+[m[32m    \\  --shell PATH    shell to run (default $SHELL)[m
[32m+[m[32m    \\  --frame-stats   print frame timing to stderr once a second[m
[32m+[m[32m    \\  --screenshot F  save the frame drawn one second in as a BMP[m
[32m+[m[32m    \\  -h, --help      this message[m
[32m+[m[32m    \\[m
[32m+[m[32m    \\Keys:[m
[32m+[m[32m    \\  Cmd +/-/0       font size[m
[32m+[m[32m    \\  Cmd V           paste[m
[32m+[m[32m    \\  Cmd K           clear[m
[32m+[m[32m    \\  Wheel           scroll history[m
[32m+[m[32m    \\[m
[32m+[m[32m;[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m/// Returns null when `--help` was asked for, so the caller decides how to[m
[32m+[m[32m/// exit rather than this file calling `std.process.exit` and taking the[m
[32m+[m[32m/// tests with it.[m
[32m+[m[32mpub fn parseArgs(argv: []const [*:0]const u8) ?Options {[m
[32m+[m[32m    var opts = Options{};[m
[32m+[m[32m    var i: usize = 1; // skip argv[0][m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    while (i < argv.len) : (i += 1) {[m
[32m+[m[32m        const arg = std.mem.span(argv[i]);[m
[32m+[m[32m        if (std.mem.eql(u8, arg, "--font-size")) {[m
[32m+[m[32m            i += 1;[m
[32m+[m[32m            if (i >= argv.len) break;[m
[32m+[m[32m            opts.font_size = parseFontSize(std.mem.span(argv[i])) orelse opts.font_size;[m
[32m+[m[32m        } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, arg, "--shell")) {[m
[32m+[m[32m            i += 1;[m
[32m+[m[32m            if (i >= argv.len) break;[m
[32m+[m[32m            opts.shell = std.mem.span(argv[i]);[m
[32m+[m[32m        } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, arg, "--frame-stats")) {[m
[32m+[m[32m            opts.frame_stats = true;[m
[32m+[m[32m        } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, arg, "--screenshot")) {[m
[32m+[m[32m            i += 1;[m
[32m+[m[32m            if (i >= argv.len) break;[m
[32m+[m[32m            opts.screenshot = std.mem.span(argv[i]);[m
[32m+[m[32m        } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, arg, "--size")) {[m
[32m+[m[32m            i += 1;[m
[32m+[m[32m            if (i >= argv.len) break;[m
[32m+[m[32m            if (parseSize(std.mem.span(argv[i]))) |size| {[m
[32m+[m[32m                opts.cols = size.cols;[m
[32m+[m[32m                opts.rows = size.rows;[m
[32m+[m[32m            }[m
[32m+[m[32m        } else if (std.mem.eql(u8, arg, "--help") or std.mem.eql(u8, arg, "-h")) {[m
[32m+[m[32m            return null;[m
[32m+[m[32m        }[m
[32m+[m[32m    }[m
[32m+[m[32m    return opts;[m
[32m+[m[32m}[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m[32m// Tests[m
[32m+[m[32m// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mconst testing = std.testing;[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mtest "a size spec parses into a grid" {[m
[32m+[m[32m    const got = parseSize("200x60").?;[m
[32m+[m[32m    try testing.expectEqual(@as(u32, 200), got.cols);[m
[32m+[m[32m    try testing.expectEqual(@as(u32, 60), got.rows);[m
[32m+[m[32m}[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mtest "a size spec is clamped at both ends" {[m
[32m+[m[32m    // The regression: `init_cols * cell_w + pad * 2` is computed as a u32[m
[32m+[m[32m    // and cast to i32, so a large enough column count panicked on overflow[m
[32m+[m[32m    // inside Renderer.init before it could draw anything.[m
[32m+[m[32m    const huge = parseSize("4000000000x30").?;[m
[32m+[m[32m    try testing.expectEqual(@as(u32, max_dim), huge.cols);[m
[32m+[m[32m    try testing.expectEqual(@as(u32, 30), huge.rows);[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    const zero = parseSize("0x0").?;[m
[32m+[m[32m    try testing.expectEqual(@as(u32, 1), zero.cols);[m
[32m+[m[32m    try testing.expectEqual(@as(u32, 1), zero.rows);[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    // Past what a u32 can hold at all, so parseInt itself refuses.[m
[32m+[m[32m    try testing.expectEqual(@as(?Size, null), parseSize("99999999999x30"));[m
[32m+[m[32m}[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mtest "a malformed size spec is declined whole" {[m
[32m+[m[32m    try testing.expectEqual(@as(?Size, null), parseSize("80"));[m
[32m+[m[32m    try testing.expectEqual(@as(?Size, null), parseSize("80xwide"));[m
[32m+[m[32m    try testing.expectEqual(@as(?Size, null), parseSize("widex24"));[m
[32m+[m[32m    try testing.expectEqual(@as(?Size, null), parseSize(""));[m
[32m+[m[32m    try testing.expectEqual(@as(?Size, null), parseSize("x"));[m
[32m+[m[32m    try testing.expectEqual(@as(?Size, null), parseSize("-5x10"));[m
[32m+[m[32m}[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mtest "font size is held to the range the keyboard enforces" {[m
[32m+[m[32m    try testing.expectEqual(@as(?u32, 18), parseFontSize("18"));[m
[32m+[m[32m    try testing.expectEqual(@as(?u32, max_font_size), parseFontSize("100000"));[m
[32m+[m[32m    try testing.expectEqual(@as(?u32, min_font_size), parseFontSize("1"));[m
[32m+[m[32m    try testing.expectEqual(@as(?u32, null), parseFontSize("big"));[m
[32m+[m[32m}[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mtest "argv is parsed into options" {[m
[32m+[m[32m    const argv = [_][*:0]const u8{[m
[32m+[m[32m        "terminator", "--size",  "200x60", "--font-size", "18", "--frame-stats",[m
[32m+[m[32m        "--shell",    "/bin/sh",[m
[32m+[m[32m    };[m
[32m+[m[32m    const opts = parseArgs(&argv).?;[m
[32m+[m[32m    try testing.expectEqual(@as(u32, 200), opts.cols);[m
[32m+[m[32m    try testing.expectEqual(@as(u32, 60), opts.rows);[m
[32m+[m[32m    try testing.expectEqual(@as(u32, 18), opts.font_size);[m
[32m+[m[32m    try testing.expect(opts.frame_stats);[m
[32m+[m[32m    try testing.expectEqualStrings("/bin/sh", opts.shell.?);[m
[32m+[m[32m    try testing.expectEqual(@as(?[:0]const u8, null), opts.screenshot);[m
[32m+[m[32m}[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mtest "a flag missing its value stops rather than reading past the end" {[m
[32m+[m[32m    const argv = [_][*:0]const u8{ "terminator", "--size" };[m
[32m+[m[32m    const opts = parseArgs(&argv).?;[m
[32m+[m[32m    try testing.expectEqual(@as(u32, default_cols), opts.cols);[m
[32m+[m[32m    try testing.expectEqual(@as(u32, default_rows), opts.rows);[m
[32m+[m[32m}[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mtest "unknown arguments are ignored and --help declines to return options" {[m
[32m+[m[32m    const unknown = [_][*:0]const u8{ "terminator", "--nonsense", "--frame-stats" };[m
[32m+[m[32m    try testing.expect(parseArgs(&unknown).?.frame_stats);[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m    const help_short = [_][*:0]const u8{ "terminator", "-h" };[m
