[33mcommit fae9ad9364c27379f698eef6fcbfbc367fede4d7[m
Author: Oddur Sigurdsson <oddurs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Fri Aug 28 22:34:42 2026 -0400

    docs: add the security, testing and compatibility roadmaps (#21)
    
    Three more roadmaps, bringing the set to twelve:
    
      security.md       the threat model; a binding reply policy -- the
                        terminal never sends the child bytes derived from
                        the screen, title or clipboard; the paste guard;
                        ReleaseSafe in the release build, gated on a bench
                        number; a build you can check
      testing.md        the layers; committing the differential model and
                        mutants Sprint R's review built by hand; the golden
                        checksum the bench already prints; fuzzing in CI;
                        replay of real programs; gating the bench by ratio
      compatibility.md  Linux, Windows and the browser as second
                        implementations of the Platform and Pty seams; what
                        "platform" means on each OS under the ownership
                        rule; a generated program matrix
    
    The compatibility claim was checked rather than assumed: the unit-test
    binaries of vt, grid, terminal, input and theme build for
    x86_64-linux-gnu, x86_64-windows-gnu and wasm32-wasi from this Mac with
    `zig test --test-no-exec`, unchanged.
    
    correctness.md's C5 moves to testing.md; platform.md's P5 and its
    "Windows is a different program" line hand off to compatibility.md;
    agentic.md's A6 points at S4; priorities.md and the README list all
    three and add the short early sprints (S0, T0, M0) beside the order.
    
    
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015A84EWxkDNg8oUXUHgS32P
    
    Co-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

