[1mdiff --git a/docs/roadmap/compatibility.md b/docs/roadmap/compatibility.md[m
[1mnew file mode 100644[m
[1mindex 0000000..2f2e593[m
[1m--- /dev/null[m
[1m+++ b/docs/roadmap/compatibility.md[m
[36m@@ -0,0 +1,225 @@[m
[32m+[m[32m# Compatibility roadmap[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mOther machines, and other programs. Linux, Windows and the browser on[m
[32m+[m[32mone side; shells, multiplexers, editors and agents on the other. Sized[m
[32m+[m[32mfor one person at 8–12 focused hours a week. Sprint prefix: **M**.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mArbiter: **the CI matrix and the compatibility matrix.** A platform is[m
[32m+[m[32msupported when its row in CI is green on every PR; a program is[m
[32m+[m[32msupported when its recording in the replay suite ([T2](testing.md))[m
[32m+[m[32mhas a golden that passes. Neither is a claim anyone makes by hand.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe [priorities](priorities.md) say *macOS first, finished, then[m
[32m+[m[32melsewhere*, and that holds. What this page adds is that "elsewhere" is[m
[32m+[m[32mdesigned for now — the seams that make the port a second implementation[m
[32m+[m[32mrather than a rewrite are the seams [D4](dependencies.md) is already[m
[32m+[m[32mdrawing — and that the core is proven portable today, in CI, so the[m
[32m+[m[32mport never has to start by discovering what was accidentally[m
[32m+[m[32mmac-specific.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Where we are[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mMeasured on 2026-08-28: `zig test --test-no-exec` builds the unit-test[m
[32m+[m[32mbinaries of `vt`, `grid`, `terminal`, `input` and `theme` for[m
[32m+[m[32m`x86_64-linux-gnu`, `x86_64-windows-gnu` and `wasm32-wasi`, from this[m
[32m+[m[32mMac, with no changes. The core is portable now; only the edges are not.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| | Today | Where |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|---|[m
[32m+[m[32m| The core (`vt`, `grid`, `terminal`, `input`, `theme`, `stats`, `bench`) | `std` only. **Builds for Linux, Windows and wasm today.** Runs on the Ubuntu runner every PR, as the bench | `build.zig` bench job |[m
[32m+[m[32m| PTY | `forkpty` from `util.h` — macOS and the BSDs. Linux has the same call in `pty.h`; Windows has ConPTY, a different shape | `pty.zig` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Fonts | Hard-coded `/System/Library/Fonts` paths; FreeType | `font.zig` `font_candidates` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Window, input, GPU | SDL3 — portable, and being replaced by AppKit and Metal ([D4](dependencies.md)) behind a `Platform` interface | `main.zig`, `render.zig` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Windows | Named as "a different program" in [platform.md](platform.md). **Revised here:** the core is the same program; the platform layer is different, which is what the platform layer is for | — |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Linux | Gated in [P5](platform.md) on the Mac experience being complete. Still true; this page is the plan for when the gate opens | — |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Programs | Verified by use: zsh, `vim`, `less`, `htop`, `tmux`. No matrix, no recordings | — |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Terminfo | `xterm-256color`; `TERM_PROGRAM=terminator` | `pty.zig` |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## What "platform" means on each OS[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe [ownership rule](dependencies.md) — link only the platform — needs[m
[32m+[m[32ma definition per platform, written down before anyone links a[m
[32m+[m[32mconvenience.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| | Window and input | GPU | PTY | Fonts | Notify |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|---|---|---|---|[m
[32m+[m[32m| macOS | AppKit | Metal | `forkpty` (libc) | scan `/System/Library/Fonts`, `~/Library/Fonts` | UserNotifications |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Linux | `libwayland-client`, `libxkbcommon`; XWayland covers X11 | OpenGL via EGL — Mesa is the platform's GL; Vulkan only if a number asks | `forkpty` (glibc/musl) | scan the XDG font dirs, `~/.fonts` — no fontconfig, we parse `name` tables ourselves | D-Bus `org.freedesktop.Notifications`, via a subprocess to `notify-send` first |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Windows | Win32 (`user32`), IMM32 for IME | Direct3D 11, HLSL compiled at runtime by `d3dcompiler_47` — no build tool | ConPTY (`CreatePseudoConsole`) | scan `C:\Windows\Fonts` | `FlashWindowEx`; toasts later |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Browser | a 200-line JS harness | `<canvas>` | none — a scripted source | the browser's | none |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEverything in the table is shipped by the OS or its display stack.[m
[32m+[m[32mNothing is fetched, vendored or built from a third party.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## The sprints[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### M0 — Prove the core is portable, on every PR (half a week)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Cross-compile in CI.** The Ubuntu job builds the unit tests for[m
[32m+[m[32m  `x86_64-linux`, `aarch64-linux`, `x86_64-windows` and `wasm32-wasi`,[m
[32m+[m[32m  and runs the Linux ones natively. The Windows ones run on a[m
[32m+[m[32m  `windows-latest` row. None of this needs a display or a PTY.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **End-to-end on Linux.** [T0](testing.md) drops SDL from the e2e[m
[32m+[m[32m  module and switches `pty.zig` to `pty.h` under Linux; the Ubuntu row[m
[32m+[m[32m  gains the e2e suite.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **A `Platform` and a `Pty` seam, named.** Not implemented for a new[m
[32m+[m[32m  OS — just the two interfaces D4 is defining, with a comment on each[m
[32m+[m[32m  saying what a second implementation may assume. The seam exists so[m
[32m+[m[32m  M2 and M3 are second implementations.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Why here:* half a week, and it turns "the core is portable" from a[m
[32m+[m[32msentence into a check. After it, nothing mac-specific can creep into[m
[32m+[m[32m`vt`, `grid`, `terminal` or `input` without a red row.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Done when:* the CI matrix has Ubuntu and Windows rows for the core,[m
[32m+[m[32mand a deliberate `@cImport("util.h")` in `terminal.zig` fails them.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Risk:* none.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### M1 — The headless platform (half a week, with C0)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mA third implementation of `Platform`, `platform/headless.zig`: no[m
[32m+[m[32mwindow, no GPU, a fake clipboard, events from a script. It is what[m
[32m+[m[32m[C0](correctness.md)'s conformance harness, [T2](testing.md)'s replay[m
[32m+[m[32mmode, [A6](agentic.md)'s `--headless` and the browser build all drive.[m
[32m+[m[32mThe renderer's vertex buffer still gets built — the gallery's diff[m
[32m+[m[32mneeds it — and `gpu_read_pixels` returns a CPU rasterization of the[m
[32m+[m[32mquads, which is a few dozen lines since every quad is an axis-aligned[m
[32m+[m[32mrectangle over one texture.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Done when:* `zig build test` runs the e2e suite and the gallery[m
[32m+[m[32magainst the headless platform on Linux with no display.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Risk:* low.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### M2 — Linux (three to four weeks) — **gated**[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mWayland-native, with XWayland for the X11 case rather than a second[m
[32m+[m[32mbackend; a from-scratch X11 client is a second sprint's worth of code[m
[32m+[m[32mfor a shrinking audience.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- `platform/wayland.c`: `xdg-shell` for the window, `wl_seat` keyboard[m
[32m+[m[32m  through `xkbcommon` for keymaps, `text-input-v3` for IME,[m
[32m+[m[32m  `fractional-scale-v1` and `viewporter` for the 1.5× case,[m
[32m+[m[32m  `wl_data_device` for the clipboard, `cursor-shape-v1` for the I-beam.[m
[32m+[m[32m  The protocol XML is committed and the C bindings generated at build[m
[32m+[m[32m  by `wayland-scanner`, which is a tool, not a link.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `platform/gpu_gl.c`: the same six functions as `gpu.m`, over EGL and[m
[32m+[m[32m  OpenGL 3.3 core. The shader is GLSL compiled at runtime from a string[m
[32m+[m[32m  — the same choice D0 made for Metal, for the same reason: no shader[m
[32m+[m[32m  compiler in the build.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Fonts: [D1](dependencies.md)'s discovery scans[m
[32m+[m[32m  `/usr/share/fonts`, `/usr/local/share/fonts`, `~/.local/share/fonts`[m
[32m+[m[32m  and `~/.fonts`; the default family list is DejaVu Sans Mono,[m
[32m+[m[32m  Liberation Mono, Noto Sans Mono, Cascadia Code — all `glyf`.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Notifications through `notify-send` as a subprocess; a hand-written[m
[32m+[m[32m  D-Bus client is on the list only if that proves inadequate.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Packaging: a tarball and an AppImage from the release workflow;[m
[32m+[m[32m  Flatpak when someone asks; distro packages never from here.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Gate:* every sprint labelled "next" on [experience.md](experience.md)[m
[32m+[m[32mlanded, and someone on Linux has asked in an issue. Both.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Done when:* the e2e suite, the gallery and the replay suite are green[m
[32m+[m[32mon the Ubuntu row *with* the Wayland platform under a headless[m
[32m+[m[32mcompositor; a Linux user has run it for a week and filed what they[m
[32m+[m[32mfound.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Risk:* medium to high. IME under `text-input-v3` and fractional[m
[32m+[m[32mscaling are the two places Wayland clients go wrong; both have a[m
[32m+[m[32mgallery capture or an e2e test waiting for them.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### M3 — Windows (four to six weeks) — **gated**[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe largest port, because the PTY is a different shape and the input[m
[32m+[m[32mmodel is too.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- `pty_win.zig`: `CreatePseudoConsole` with a pair of pipes,[m
[32m+[m[32m  `ResizePseudoConsole`, `ClosePseudoConsole`; the child is started[m
[32m+[m[32m  with the pseudo-console attribute on its `STARTUPINFOEX`. ConPTY[m
[32m+[m[32m  speaks VT on both sides, so `vt.Parser` and `input.zig` are[m
[32m+[m[32m  unchanged — which is the point of ConPTY.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `platform/win32.c`: a window class, `WM_KEYDOWN`/`WM_CHAR` to[m
[32m+[m[32m  `input.zig`, IMM32 composition for IME, per-monitor-v2 DPI[m
[32m+[m[32m  awareness, the clipboard, `WM_MOUSEWHEEL` with precise deltas.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `platform/gpu_d3d11.c`: the same six functions, over a swap chain,[m
[32m+[m[32m  with the HLSL compiled at runtime.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Fonts: scan `C:\Windows\Fonts`; defaults Cascadia Mono, Consolas —[m
[32m+[m[32m  both `glyf`. Windows users expect ClearType's weight; D0's linear[m
[32m+[m[32m  blending plus [X1](experience.md)'s measured darkening is the answer,[m
[32m+[m[32m  and the gallery says whether it is enough.[m
[32m+[m[32m- The shell: PowerShell by default, `cmd` and WSL by config. `TERM` is[m
[32m+[m[32m  not a Windows convention; `TERM_PROGRAM` still is ours to set.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Packaging: a zip and a `winget` manifest; MSIX if anyone asks.[m
[32m+[m[32m  Authenticode signing costs money and is a decision for then.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Gate:* M2 shipped, and someone on Windows has asked.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Done when:* the same three suites are green on the Windows row; a[m
[32m+[m[32mWindows user has run it for a week.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Risk:* high. IMM32 and the ConPTY resize dance are the known traps.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### M4 — The core in a browser (one week) — **gated**[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m`vt`, `grid` and `terminal` compile to `wasm32` today. A 200-line JS[m
[32m+[m[32mharness feeds keystrokes in, calls `feed`, and paints the grid to a[m
[32m+[m[32m`<canvas>` from an exported cell array. On the website[m
[32m+[m[32m([W](website.md)) it is a page of its own — the site's no-script rule[m
[32m+[m[32mholds everywhere else — where a visitor types into a real terminator[m
[32m+[m[32mcore before installing anything.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIt is also a portability proof with teeth: a `std` feature that does[m
[32m+[m[32mnot exist on `wasm32-freestanding` fails the build.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Gate:* [W1](website.md) exists, and the maintainer wants a demo.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Done when:* the page runs the `altscreen` corpus and shows the same[m
[32m+[m[32mgrid the golden test records.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Risk:* low.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### M5 — The compatibility matrix (ongoing, derived)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m`docs/compatibility.md`, generated — not written — from the replay[m
[32m+[m[32msuite ([T2](testing.md)): one row per recording, one column per[m
[32m+[m[32mplatform, a cell that says *golden passes* or links the failing[m
[32m+[m[32msequence. Rows to record first:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- shells: zsh, bash, fish, nushell; PowerShell on Windows[m
[32m+[m[32m- multiplexers: tmux, zellij, screen[m
[32m+[m[32m- editors: vim, neovim, helix, `emacs -nw`[m
[32m+[m[32m- TUIs: htop, btop, lazygit, k9s[m
[32m+[m[32m- agents: the [A0](agentic.md) recordings[m
[32m+[m[32m- transports: over `ssh`, over `mosh`, inside tmux over ssh[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mA row is added by adding a recording; a row goes green by fixing what[m
[32m+[m[32mthe golden shows. The page says when it was generated and from which[m
[32m+[m[32mcommit.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Done when:* the page exists and is regenerated by CI on every merge.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Risk:* none, as long as nobody edits it by hand.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Why this order[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **M0 now**, because it is half a week and it fences the core.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **M1 with C0**, because they are the same binary.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **M2 and M3 gated**, per the priorities, and in that order — Linux is[m
[32m+[m[32m  a second implementation of seams that exist; Windows also changes the[m
[32m+[m[32m  PTY.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **M4 whenever the site wants it.**[m
[32m+[m[32m- **M5 as soon as T2 has recordings**; it is a report, not a sprint.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Not on this plan[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **GTK, Qt, or any toolkit.** The platform layer talks to the display[m
[32m+[m[32m  server, as it talks to AppKit on the Mac.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **A native X11 backend.** XWayland.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **iOS, Android, the Apple TV.** No shell to run.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Supporting a program by special-casing it.** If `tmux` needs a[m
[32m+[m[32m  sequence, the sequence is implemented per its spec and every program[m
[32m+[m[32m  gets it; nothing checks `TERM_PROGRAM` of the child.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Distro packaging.** Tarball, AppImage, cask, zip. Package[m
[32m+[m[32m  maintainers know their distributions better than this repository[m
[32m+[m[32m  does.[m
