[1mdiff --git a/docs/roadmap/security.md b/docs/roadmap/security.md[m
[1mnew file mode 100644[m
[1mindex 0000000..b3c995f[m
[1m--- /dev/null[m
[1m+++ b/docs/roadmap/security.md[m
[36m@@ -0,0 +1,237 @@[m
[32m+[m[32m# Security roadmap[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mA terminal parses hostile bytes for a living. Anything that writes to it —[m
[32m+[m[32m`cat` on a downloaded file, a compromised host over `ssh`, an agent[m
[32m+[m[32mprinting whatever a web page told it to — controls the input to the[m
[32m+[m[32mparser, and the parser's job is to make sure that input can paint the[m
[32m+[m[32mscreen and nothing else. Sized for one person at 8–12 focused hours a[m
[32m+[m[32mweek. Sprint prefix: **S**.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mArbiter: **the policy table and the fuzzer.** Every sequence that could[m
[32m+[m[32mcarry bytes *out* of the terminal — a reply, a clipboard write, a link, a[m
[32m+[m[32mpaste — has a row in the table below saying what is allowed, and a test[m
[32m+[m[32mthat proves the forbidden case emits nothing. Every parser of untrusted[m
[32m+[m[32minput has a fuzz target that runs in CI.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## The threat model[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFour attackers, in the order they matter.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. **A program writing to the terminal.** It wants to run a command as[m
[32m+[m[32m   the user (inject bytes into the shell's input), read something (the[m
[32m+[m[32m   clipboard, the screen, the title), or spoof the display (hide what[m
[32m+[m[32m   was really run). This is the one `SECURITY.md` already describes and[m
[32m+[m[32m   the one every sprint below serves.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. **A file the user opens.** A font in `~/Library/Fonts`, a config[m
[32m+[m[32m   file, a corpus, a PNG inside an emoji font. After[m
[32m+[m[32m   [D1](dependencies.md) and [D2](dependencies.md) those parsers are[m
[32m+[m[32m   ours, and ours to fuzz.[m
[32m+[m[32m3. **A local process.** Once [A6](agentic.md)'s socket exists, another[m
[32m+[m[32m   user's process on the same machine must not be able to type into a[m
[32m+[m[32m   tab.[m
[32m+[m[32m4. **The build.** What lands in the release binary and how anyone could[m
[32m+[m[32m   check.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mNot an attacker: the user at the keyboard. `--shell`, `--screenshot`[m
[32m+[m[32mand `--font` take what they are given; if you can pass arguments you[m
[32m+[m[32mcan already run anything, as `SECURITY.md` says.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Where we are[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| | Today | Where |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|---|[m
[32m+[m[32m| Release build | **ReleaseFast** — bounds and overflow checks off in the code that parses hostile bytes | `release.yml`, `ci.yml` matrix has no ReleaseSafe row |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Replies to the child | DA1 and DSR 5/6 only. **Nothing echoes screen, title or clipboard content back.** The property to keep | `deviceStatusReport`, `deviceAttributes` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Title query (XTWINOPS 21) | Not implemented — correct; it is the classic injection vector | — |[m
[32m+[m[32m| OSC 52 clipboard | Not implemented. [A2](agentic.md) adds write, and read only behind a config key | `oscDispatch` `else` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Paste | Bracketed when the app asks. **Otherwise raw**: a clipboard containing `\n` executes on paste; one containing `\x1b` is parsed as typed | `handleKey` `Cmd V` → `sendToPty` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Hyperlinks, path open | Not implemented; [A4](agentic.md) needs a policy before it exists | — |[m
[32m+[m[32m| DCS, APC, SOS, PM | Swallowed to ST, never answered | `vt.zig` `string_ignore` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Notification text | Not implemented; [A1](agentic.md) will put child-controlled text in a system notification | — |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Child environment | Inherits the parent's; sets `TERM`, `COLORTERM`, `TERM_PROGRAM`, unsets `LINES`/`COLUMNS` | `pty.zig` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Network | **None.** [P3](platform.md) adds one request, behind a key | — |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Font files | Parsed by FreeType; ours after D1 | `font.zig` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Fuzzing | None | — |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Actions | Pinned by major tag (`@v5`), not SHA; Dependabot keeps them current (its first PR is open) | `.github/workflows/`, `dependabot.yml` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Build inputs | Zig pinned to 0.16.0; SDL3 and FreeType at whatever Homebrew has that day | `release.yml` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Reproducibility | Not checked | — |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Signing | None ([P1](platform.md)) | — |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Disclosure | `SECURITY.md`: private advisories, a week to acknowledge, scope stated | `SECURITY.md` |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe strongest line in that table is the third one, and it is there by[m
[32m+[m[32maccident of not having implemented the queries yet. S0 makes it a rule.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## The policy table[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe rule: **the terminal never sends the child bytes derived from screen[m
[32m+[m[32mcontent, the title, the clipboard, or another tab.** Replies carry only[m
[32m+[m[32mwhat the child could already know — modes, capabilities, cursor[m
[32m+[m[32mposition.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| Sequence | Direction | Policy |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|---|[m
[32m+[m[32m| DA1, DA2, XTVERSION, DECRQM, DSR 5/6, XTWINOPS 14/16/18 | reply | Allowed: capabilities, modes, geometry. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| XTWINOPS 21 (report title), 20 (report icon) | reply | **Never.** Title is child-controlled; reporting it is an injection channel. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| DECRQSS, DECRQCRA (checksum of screen), XTGETTCAP | reply | Refused until a program is found that needs it; DECRQCRA never — it reads the screen. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| OSC 52 write | out to clipboard | Allowed by default; capped at 1 MiB; config key to disable. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| OSC 52 read | reply | **Off by default.** Key to enable; the docs say what it means. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| OSC 8 link | on click only | Schemes `http`, `https`, `mailto`; `file` with a confirm; anything else shown and not opened. The URI is displayed before opening. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Path open ([A4](agentic.md)) | subprocess | Editor invoked with `--` and an absolute path; never through a shell. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| OSC 0/2 title, OSC 9/777 notification text | to the OS | C0 and C1 stripped; length-capped; never interpreted. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Paste, bracketed mode off | into the PTY | **Guarded** (S1): `\n`, `\r`, `\x1b` or any C0 prompts once, shows what will be sent. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Paste, bracketed mode on | into the PTY | Sent inside the markers; a `\x1b[201~` inside the payload is stripped so the paste cannot close its own bracket. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| DCS, APC, SOS, PM | — | Swallowed. Stays that way. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Remote-control socket ([A6](agentic.md)) | in | Token, 0600, per user; see S4. |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## The sprints[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### S0 — The threat model and the table, made binding (two days)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mMove the two sections above into `docs/security.md` (the roadmap keeps[m
[32m+[m[32mthe sprints; the policy needs a permanent home) and give every row a[m
[32m+[m[32mtest: for each forbidden reply, a unit test feeds the sequence and[m
[32m+[m[32masserts `replies` is empty; for each allowed one, asserts the reply[m
[32m+[m[32mcontains no byte from the screen. `SECURITY.md` links the policy and[m
[32m+[m[32msays the rule in one sentence.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Why here:* before [A2](agentic.md) and [C1](correctness.md) add the[m
[32m+[m[32mfirst batch of new replies. A policy written after the queries exist is[m
[32m+[m[32ma list of exceptions.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Done when:* the table has a test per row, and `SECURITY.md`'s scope[m
[32m+[m[32msection cites it.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Risk:* none.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### S1 — Safe defaults for untrusted output (one week)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **The paste guard.** When bracketed paste is off and the clipboard[m
[32m+[m[32m  holds a newline, a carriage return, an escape or any other C0, show[m
[32m+[m[32m  one line in the grid — *paste contains 3 lines and 1 control[m
[32m+[m[32m  character; ⏎ to send, Esc to cancel* — and send only on confirm. A[m
[32m+[m[32m  config key disables it. kitty, iTerm2 and WezTerm all ship a version[m
[32m+[m[32m  of this; the attack it stops is a web page that puts[m
[32m+[m[32m  `innocuous\ncurl … | sh\n` on the clipboard.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Bracket integrity.** Strip `\x1b[201~` from a bracketed payload.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Title and notification hygiene.** Strip C0/C1, cap at 1 KiB, before[m
[32m+[m[32m  `setTitle` or [A1](agentic.md)'s notification call.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **The OSC 52 keys**, the OSC 8 scheme list and the confirm, landing[m
[32m+[m[32m  with [A2](agentic.md) and [A4](agentic.md) rather than after them —[m
[32m+[m[32m  this sprint owns the policy; those own the feature.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Done when:* an e2e test pastes a two-line clipboard with bracketed[m
[32m+[m[32mmode off and asserts nothing reached the PTY until confirm; a unit test[m
[32m+[m[32mproves a bracketed payload cannot close its own bracket.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Risk:* low. The guard is a UI decision more than a security one, and[m
[32m+[m[32mthe config key is for the people who disagree.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### S2 — Memory safety in the release build (one week) — **gated on a number**[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mBuild with `ReleaseSafe` and run the bench and `--frame-stats`. Zig's[m
[32m+[m[32msafety checks — bounds, overflow, unreachable — turn a hostile-bytes bug[m
[32m+[m[32mfrom silent corruption into a panic, which for a terminal is the right[m
[32m+[m[32mfailure. The cost is unknown until measured, and the plan says so.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Gate:* if `ReleaseSafe` is within **10%** of `ReleaseFast` on every[m
[32m+[m[32mcorpus, the release build becomes `ReleaseSafe` and the matrix gains[m
[32m+[m[32mthe row. If it is not, find where — almost certainly the printable-run[m
[32m+[m[32mloop [Sprint 4](completed/sprint-4-print-run.md) built — and mark that[m
[32m+[m[32mone block `@setRuntimeSafety(false)` with a comment naming the fuzz[m
[32m+[m[32mtarget that covers it. Everything else ships safe.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEither way, this sprint adds `ReleaseSafe` to CI, and hands[m
[32m+[m[32m[testing.md](testing.md)'s T1 its list of fuzz targets: `vt.Parser`,[m
[32m+[m[32m`Terminal` operations, the config parser ([E5](essentials.md)), the[m
[32m+[m[32mfont parser ([D1](dependencies.md)), the PNG decoder[m
[32m+[m[32m([D2](dependencies.md)), the GSUB reader ([D3](dependencies.md)), and[m
[32m+[m[32mthe remote-control protocol ([A6](agentic.md)). Every parser of bytes[m
[32m+[m[32mthe user did not type.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Done when:* the bench numbers for both modes are in this file; the[m
[32m+[m[32mrelease workflow builds whichever the gate chose; the CI matrix has[m
[32m+[m[32mthree optimize rows.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Risk:* low. The worst case is a documented 10% and a fuzzed hot loop.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### S3 — The build you can check (half a week)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Pin Actions by SHA.** Dependabot already groups and bumps them; it[m
[32m+[m[32m  bumps SHAs too. The open Dependabot PR is the proof it works.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Pin what Homebrew installs** in `release.yml` — formula versions,[m
[32m+[m[32m  not "latest" — until [D5](dependencies.md) removes the question.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Reproducible release.** The release workflow builds twice, in two[m
[32m+[m[32m  jobs, and fails if the SHA-256 differs. Zig is deterministic for the[m
[32m+[m[32m  same toolchain and inputs; assert it rather than assume it.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Least privilege in workflows.** `permissions:` blocks exist in[m
[32m+[m[32m  both; make CI's read-only and release's `contents: write` the only[m
[32m+[m[32m  grant.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **The signing key** ([P1](platform.md)) lives in a GitHub environment[m
[32m+[m[32m  with a required reviewer — the maintainer — so a workflow change[m
[32m+[m[32m  cannot silently sign.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **An SBOM that fits on one line**: after D5, the link line from[m
[32m+[m[32m  `otool -L` and the Zig version, printed in the release notes.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Done when:* `grep uses: .github/workflows/*.yml` shows only SHAs; a[m
[32m+[m[32mrelease run shows two matching checksums.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Risk:* none.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### S4 — The remote-control boundary (half a week, with A6) — **gated on A6**[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe socket is a way for a process to type into the terminal, so it is[m
[32m+[m[32mheld to the same rule as everything else on this page.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- A per-user directory, mode 0700, socket 0600.[m
[32m+[m[32m- A random token, generated at start, passed to children in the[m
[32m+[m[32m  environment and required on every connection. A process that did not[m
[32m+[m[32m  start under this terminal does not have it.[m
[32m+[m[32m- A size cap per message and a rate cap per connection.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `--no-remote` disables it; `--headless` binds nothing unless asked.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `send` into a tab is subject to the paste guard's rules — a control[m
[32m+[m[32m  character from the socket is a control character.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Done when:* an e2e test connects without the token and is refused;[m
[32m+[m[32mwith it, is accepted; a second user on the machine cannot connect at[m
[32m+[m[32mall.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Risk:* low in code. The design is the whole thing, and it is above.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### S5 — Least privilege in the app (half a week, with P1)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Entitlements: none beyond the hardened runtime's defaults. A PTY[m
[32m+[m[32m  needs nothing. After [D5](dependencies.md) there are no dylibs, so no[m
[32m+[m[32m  library-validation exception.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `Info.plist` usage descriptions: absent, because nothing is used.[m
[32m+[m[32m- The one network call ([P3](platform.md)) is documented in[m
[32m+[m[32m  `SECURITY.md` as the one network call, with its config key.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `--screenshot` and the panic corpus ([C4](correctness.md)) write only[m
[32m+[m[32m  where told, and the panic corpus only when asked.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Done when:* `codesign -d --entitlements -` on the release prints the[m
[32m+[m[32mminimal set, and the release notes quote it.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Risk:* none.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Why this order[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **S0 before A2 and C1**, so the first new replies are written against[m
[32m+[m[32m  a policy instead of becoming one.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **S1 early** because the paste guard closes the one attack a user can[m
[32m+[m[32m  meet today, and it is a week.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **S2 gated on a number** the bench can give in an afternoon.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **S3 whenever**; it is configuration.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **S4 and S5 ride their sprints.**[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Not on this plan[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Sandboxing the terminal.** A terminal exists to run a shell with[m
[32m+[m[32m  the user's privileges; a sandbox that allowed that would not be one.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Filtering what programs may print.** The parser is the filter. A[m
[32m+[m[32m  sequence is either handled, ignored, or swallowed; there is no[m
[32m+[m[32m  allowlist of programs.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Auditing SDL3 or FreeType.** They are being removed[m
[32m+[m[32m  ([dependencies.md](dependencies.md)); the time goes to fuzzing what[m
[32m+[m[32m  replaces them.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **A bug bounty.** `SECURITY.md` promises a straight answer within a[m
[32m+[m[32m  week, which is what a personal project can honestly offer.[m
[1mdiff --git a/docs/roadmap/testing.md b/docs/roadmap/testing.md[m
[1mnew file mode 100644[m
[1mindex 0000000..610cd56[m
[1m--- /dev/null[m
[1m+++ b/docs/roadmap/testing.md[m
[36m@@ -0,0 +1,197 @@[m
[32m+[m[32m# Testing roadmap[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mHow we know it works. Every roadmap in this directory names an arbiter —[m
[32m+[m[32ma bench, a gallery, a corpus, a harness — and this page is where those[m
[32m+[m[32marbiters are built, kept fast, and made to run on every PR. Sized for[m
[32m+[m[32mone person at 8–12 focused hours a week. Sprint prefix: **T**.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mArbiter: **CI, under five minutes, on every PR,** with every other[m
[32m+[m[32mroadmap's arbiter reporting in it. A test that only runs on the[m
[32m+[m[32mmaintainer's machine is a test that runs when the maintainer remembers.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## The layers[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe suite is split by what each layer can see, and the split is[m
[32m+[m[32mdeliberate — CONTRIBUTING.md already says which layer a fix belongs[m
[32m+[m[32min. This page adds what each layer is *for*.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| Layer | Sees | Catches | Speed |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|---|---|[m
[32m+[m[32m| Unit (`test` blocks in each module) | One module, no I/O | Parser transitions, grid arithmetic, key encoding | seconds |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Differential | `Terminal` against a naive reference model | Anything the ring, the run fast path or reflow gets wrong that a hand-written test did not think of | seconds |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Golden | A corpus through `Terminal`, the final grid hashed | Any change to terminal semantics, intended or not | seconds |[m
[32m+[m[32m| End-to-end (`tests.zig`) | A real shell on a real PTY | Everything below the renderer, as a program would experience it | tens of seconds |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Gallery ([X0](experience.md)) | Rendered frames at 1× and 2× | Anything visual | a minute |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Conformance ([C0](correctness.md)) | esctest against the headless terminal | The spec | a minute |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Fuzz | Random bytes into every parser of untrusted input | Crashes, hangs, invariant violations | a minute in CI, hours locally |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Bench | Throughput and frame timing | Regressions in speed | a minute |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Where we are[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| | Today | Where |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|---|[m
[32m+[m[32m| Unit tests | 61 across six modules, in-module `test` blocks | `vt` 12, `terminal` 20, `grid` 13, `input` 10, `font` 4, `theme` 2 |[m
[32m+[m[32m| End-to-end | 8, on a real shell and PTY. **macOS only**, because the module links SDL3 although `tests.zig` imports only `vt`, `grid`, `terminal` and `pty` | `build.zig` `e2e_mod` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Bench | Six corpora, headless, ReleaseFast, on the Linux runner; **non-gating** because a shared runner is too noisy | `ci.yml` bench job |[m
[32m+[m[32m| A checksum | `zig build bench` already prints a checksum of the final grid state across every corpus — **a golden test nobody asserts on** | `bench/baseline.txt` last line |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Differential model | Built in review for Sprint R (400 seeds × 200 ops against a naive reference), **not committed** | [sprint R record](completed/sprint-r-screen-ring.md) |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Mutation testing | Done by hand once, seven mutants, one survived until a test was added; **not repeatable** | same |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Fuzzing | None | — |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Gallery, conformance | Not yet ([X0](experience.md), [C0](correctness.md)) | — |[m
[32m+[m[32m| CI matrix | `zig fmt`; Debug and ReleaseFast on macOS 14 and 15; bench on Ubuntu. No ReleaseSafe, no Linux tests, no Windows | `ci.yml` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| CI time | ~2 m 20 s for the slowest job | recent runs |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Coverage | None | — |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Flake policy | None needed yet; none written | — |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mTwo of the most valuable tests this project has ever run — the[m
[32m+[m[32mdifferential model and the mutants — exist only in a markdown record.[m
[32m+[m[32mT0 is about that.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## The sprints[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### T0 — Commit what already proved things (one week)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **The differential model.** A `RefTerminal` in `src/test/ref.zig`: a[m
[32m+[m[32m  plain 2-D array of cells with the obvious implementation of every[m
[32m+[m[32m  operation — scroll by copying, insert by shifting, no ring, no fast[m
[32m+[m[32m  path. A test drives `Terminal` and `RefTerminal` with the same random[m
[32m+[m[32m  operation stream (seeded, so a failure is a seed number) and compares[m
[32m+[m[32m  grids after every step. This is the test that would have caught a[m
[32m+[m[32m  wrong ring rotation before Sprint R's reviewer had to build it, and it[m
[32m+[m[32m  is the test every future data-structure sprint — reflow[m
[32m+[m[32m  ([E4](essentials.md)), the cluster table ([C2](correctness.md)), the[m
[32m+[m[32m  region ring ([#12](https://github.com/oddurs/terminator/issues/12)) —[m
[32m+[m[32m  gets for free.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **The golden checksum.** The number `zig build bench` prints becomes[m
[32m+[m[32m  `test "corpora produce the recorded grid state"`, with the expected[m
[32m+[m[32m  value in the test. An intentional semantic change updates it in the[m
[32m+[m[32m  same PR, with the reason; an unintentional one fails.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **The mutants, as a script.** `bench/mutants/` holds one patch per[m
[32m+[m[32m  mutation from the Sprint R record; `zig build mutants` applies each,[m
[32m+[m[32m  runs the suite, and fails if any mutant *passes*. Seven to start.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **End-to-end on Linux.** Drop the SDL link from `e2e_mod`, switch[m
[32m+[m[32m  `pty.zig`'s include to `pty.h` under Linux, and add the Ubuntu row.[m
[32m+[m[32m  The bench already proves the core runs there; the e2e suite proves the[m
[32m+[m[32m  PTY layer does.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Why here:* the highest-value tests on any roadmap, and the only ones[m
[32m+[m[32mthat already exist.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Done when:* `zig build test` runs the differential model for 1,000[m
[32m+[m[32mseeds in under five seconds; the checksum is asserted; `zig build[m
[32m+[m[32mmutants` kills all seven; e2e is green on Ubuntu.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Risk:* low. The reference model is deliberately naive; the risk is[m
[32m+[m[32mmaking it clever.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### T1 — Fuzzing in CI (one week)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m`zig build fuzz` with `std.testing.fuzz`, one target per parser of[m
[32m+[m[32mbytes the user did not type — the list [S2](security.md) owns:[m
[32m+[m[32m`vt.Parser` into `Terminal`, the config parser, the font parser, the[m
[32m+[m[32mPNG decoder, the GSUB reader, the remote-control protocol, each added[m
[32m+[m[32mthe sprint its parser lands.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mInvariants, checked after every input: no panic; cursor in bounds;[m
[32m+[m[32mevery `.wide` followed by a `.spacer` and every `.spacer` preceded by a[m
[32m+[m[32m`.wide`; `pending_wrap` implies the last column; `view_offset ≤[m
[32m+[m[32mscrollback.len`; the differential model agrees. Seeds are the bench[m
[32m+[m[32mcorpora and the agent recordings, so the fuzzer starts from real input[m
[32m+[m[32mrather than noise.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**A crash becomes a test.** The fuzzer writes its reproducer to[m
[32m+[m[32m`src/test/fuzz-regressions/<hash>.bin`, and a test replays every file[m
[32m+[m[32min that directory. A bug found by fuzzing can never come back unnoticed.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mOne minute per target in CI; the maintainer's machine runs longer.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Done when:* CI shows a fuzz job per target; the regression directory[m
[32m+[m[32mexists with at least one file in it (there will be one).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Risk:* low.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### T2 — Replay: real programs, headless (one to two weeks)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mA `replay` mode of the headless terminal ([C0](correctness.md)):[m
[32m+[m[32mfeed a recording at its recorded timing, or as fast as possible, and[m
[32m+[m[32mdump the grid at the end or at marks. Two uses:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **TUI smoke tests.** Recordings of `vim`, `less`, `htop`, `tmux` and[m
[32m+[m[32m  the agent CLIs from [A0](agentic.md) doing a fixed task, each with a[m
[32m+[m[32m  golden final grid. When a sequence's handling changes, every program[m
[32m+[m[32m  that uses it says so at once. The recordings are also the bench's[m
[32m+[m[32m  seventh-through-twelfth corpora.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **The compatibility matrix** ([M5](compatibility.md)) derives its[m
[32m+[m[32m  rows from this suite instead of from memory.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Why here:* after C0 has the headless binary, and after A0 has the[m
[32m+[m[32mfirst recordings.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Done when:* ten recordings with goldens run in under thirty seconds;[m
[32m+[m[32ma deliberately broken `DECSTBM` fails the `vim` and `tmux` rows and no[m
[32m+[m[32mothers.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Risk:* low to medium. Timing-dependent programs need the "as fast as[m
[32m+[m[32mpossible" mode to be deterministic; if one is not, it is recorded[m
[32m+[m[32mwithout timing.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### T3 — Gating the bench (half a week)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe bench is non-gating because a shared runner's absolute numbers are[m
[32m+[m[32mnoise. Ratios are not: the job builds **both** the PR and its merge[m
[32m+[m[32mbase, runs them alternately in the same process lifetime, and compares.[m
[32m+[m[32mThe noise cancels; a 10% regression on any corpus fails the check, and[m
[32m+[m[32ma 10% improvement posts a comment asking whether the baseline should[m
[32m+[m[32mbe re-recorded.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m`--frame-stats` stays local — a runner with no display cannot measure[m
[32m+[m[32mpresent — but `build` can be measured headless once[m
[32m+[m[32m[D0](dependencies.md) can render to an offscreen texture, and joins the[m
[32m+[m[32mratio check then.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Done when:* a PR that adds a `std.mem.copyForwards` back into[m
[32m+[m[32m`scrollUp` fails CI.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Risk:* low. If the ratio approach is still noisy, the threshold moves[m
[32m+[m[32mbefore the idea is abandoned.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### T4 — Hygiene (ongoing, half a day a sprint)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **A time budget**, enforced: unit under 5 s, e2e under 30 s, the[m
[32m+[m[32m  whole CI under 5 minutes. A test that breaks the budget is optimised[m
[32m+[m[32m  or moved to a nightly job, never tolerated.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **A flake policy**, written before the first flake: a flaky test is a[m
[32m+[m[32m  bug with a one-week deadline, CI has no retry, and a test may be[m
[32m+[m[32m  skipped only with an issue number in the skip.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Coverage** on Linux via `kcov` over the test binaries — Zig emits[m
[32m+[m[32m  the DWARF it needs — reported per module, non-gating, so an untested[m
[32m+[m[32m  path is at least visible.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Every roadmap arbiter in one summary.** The PR summary shows: tests,[m
[32m+[m[32m  bench ratio, gallery diffs, esctest count, fuzz status. One place to[m
[32m+[m[32m  look.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Done when:* the PR summary is that one place.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Why this order[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **T0 first**, because the tests are already designed and the review[m
[32m+[m[32m  that designed them is the most careful work in the repository.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **T1 with S2**, since the fuzz list is the security roadmap's.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **T2 after C0 and A0** provide the binary and the recordings.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **T3 as soon as one perf PR would have benefited** — which, given the[m
[32m+[m[32m  history, is the next one.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **T4 is a habit**, not a sprint.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Not on this plan[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **A mocking framework.** The seams are real: the parser takes any[m
[32m+[m[32m  handler, the terminal does no I/O, the renderer draws a copy.[m
[32m+[m[32m  Nothing needs mocking.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Property-based testing beyond the differential model.** The model[m
[32m+[m[32m  *is* the property; a second framework would be a second way to say[m
[32m+[m[32m  it.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **UI automation on the real window.** The gallery renders frames[m
[32m+[m[32m  headless; the e2e suite drives the PTY. What is left — clicking on a[m
[32m+[m[32m  menu — is [D4](dependencies.md)'s acceptance checklist, by hand.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **100% coverage.** The number is reported so gaps are visible, not so[m
[32m+[m[32m  they are filled for their own sake.[m

