    docs: add the releases and website roadmaps (#20)
    
    Two more roadmaps beside the seven that landed in #19:
    
      releases.md   what a version promises, the release train, milestones
                    mapped onto the priorities order, the shape of release
                    notes, support and security policy
      website.md    the marketing site on GitHub Pages -- two hand-written
                    files and a standard-library generator, rendering only
                    what the repository already produces
    
    The releases audit found the repository describing a release that did
    not happen: CHANGELOG.md records a 0.1.0 dated today and links to a
    v0.1.0 tag, and there are no tags. V0 is a day of making that true and
    moving the version to one source of truth with a --version flag.
    
    platform.md's P2 hands release notes and versioning to releases.md;
    priorities.md and the directory README list both.
    
    
