 [m
 Stated so they do not have to be re-decided.[m
[1mdiff --git a/docs/roadmap/releases.md b/docs/roadmap/releases.md[m
[1mnew file mode 100644[m
[1mindex 0000000..751b836[m
[1m--- /dev/null[m
[1m+++ b/docs/roadmap/releases.md[m
[36m@@ -0,0 +1,200 @@[m
[32m+[m[32m# Releases roadmap[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mWhat a version number promises, when one ships, and what is written next[m
[32m+[m[32mto it. [platform.md](platform.md) covers the mechanics — bundle, signing,[m
[32m+[m[32mDMG, cask; this covers the process those mechanics serve. Sized for one[m
[32m+[m[32mperson at 8–12 focused hours a week. Sprint prefix: **V**.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mArbiter: **the tag.** A release exists when `git tag` says so, the[m
[32m+[m[32mchangelog has a section for it, `--version` prints it, and the release[m
[32m+[m[32mpage carries an artifact a fresh Mac can open. Anything less is a draft.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Where we are[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| | Today | Where |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|---|[m
[32m+[m[32m| Tagged releases | **None.** `git tag` is empty; `gh release list` is empty | — |[m
[32m+[m[32m| The changelog | Records a `0.1.0` dated 2026-08-28 and links to `v0.1.0`, **which does not exist** | `CHANGELOG.md` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| The version | `"0.1.0"`, a constant in `pty.zig` because that is where `TERM_PROGRAM_VERSION` is set. No `--version` flag | `pty.zig` `version`; `parseArgs` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Release workflow | Runs on a `v*` tag: builds, tars a bare binary, publishes with `--generate-notes` — a second set of notes, generated from PR titles, beside the hand-written changelog | `.github/workflows/release.yml` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Merge style | Squash, one PR per concern, prefixed titles (`perf:`, `docs:`, `ci:`, `bench:`) | `git log` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| CI on `main` | `zig fmt`, Debug and ReleaseFast on macOS 14 and 15, bench (non-gating) | `.github/workflows/ci.yml` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Nightly or pre-release | None | — |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Milestones | One, for the performance sprints, now closed | GitHub |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Support statement | `SECURITY.md` says how to report; nothing says which versions get a fix | `SECURITY.md` |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe bones are right: squash merges with prefixed titles are exactly what[m
[32m+[m[32mrelease notes want, and the workflow fires on a tag. What is missing is[m
[32m+[m[32mthe tag, one source of truth for the number, and a reason to cut one.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## The sprints[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### V0 — Make 0.1.0 true (one day)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **One source of truth.** The version moves to `build.zig.zon`'s[m
[32m+[m[32m  `.version` and is threaded through a build option into `--version`,[m
[32m+[m[32m  `TERM_PROGRAM_VERSION`, `--doctor` ([P4](platform.md)) and the[m
[32m+[m[32m  bundle's `Info.plist` ([P0](platform.md)). `pty.zig` stops owning it.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **`--version`** prints `terminator 0.1.0 (e0a3191)` — the tag and the[m
[32m+[m[32m  commit, so a bug report says which build.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Tag it.** `v0.1.0` on the commit the changelog describes, or the[m
[32m+[m[32m  changelog's date and link corrected to the commit that gets tagged.[m
[32m+[m[32m  Either is honest; a changelog entry for a release that never happened[m
[32m+[m[32m  is not.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **The workflow checks the changelog.** `release.yml` fails if[m
[32m+[m[32m  `CHANGELOG.md` has no section for the tag being built. The hand-written[m
[32m+[m[32m  section becomes the release body; `--generate-notes` output goes under[m
[32m+[m[32m  an "All changes" heading beneath it rather than replacing it.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Done when:* `gh release list` shows `v0.1.0`, `terminator --version`[m
[32m+[m[32mprints it, and the changelog's links resolve.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Risk:* none. This is a day of making the repository agree with itself.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### V1 — The release train (one week)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mReleases are **sprint-driven, with a monthly floor.** A tagged release[m
[32m+[m[32mships when a roadmap sprint lands that a user can feel; if a month[m
[32m+[m[32mpasses with merges and no sprint, a release ships anyway. Time-based[m
[32m+[m[32mreleases ship nothing; sprint-based ones ship something with a name.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Nightly.** Every merge to `main` builds a pre-release artifact and[m
[32m+[m[32m  updates a rolling `nightly` GitHub pre-release. `--version` on it[m
[32m+[m[32m  prints `0.2.0-dev+<sha>`. Until [P1](platform.md) has signing, the[m
[32m+[m[32m  nightly is an Actions artifact, not a download link — an unsigned[m
[32m+[m[32m  nightly is a Gatekeeper dialog, and nobody should meet the project[m
[32m+[m[32m  through one of those.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **The checklist**, in `docs/releasing.md`, run by the maintainer from[m
[32m+[m[32m  `main` and nowhere else:[m
[32m+[m[32m  1. `zig build test` green on both macOS runners.[m
[32m+[m[32m  2. `zig build bench` against `bench/baseline.txt`: no corpus more than[m
[32m+[m[32m     5% slower; re-record the baseline if anything is faster.[m
[32m+[m[32m  3. The [gallery](experience.md) diff reviewed and intentional.[m
[32m+[m[32m  4. The esctest pass count ([C0](correctness.md)) not lower than the[m
[32m+[m[32m     last release.[m
[32m+[m[32m  5. The changelog section written — see V3 for what goes in it.[m
[32m+[m[32m  6. Tag, push, watch the workflow, open the artifact on a fresh Mac.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Stable is a nightly the maintainer has used for a week.** No[m
[32m+[m[32m  separate beta channel; the person cutting the release is the beta.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Rollback** is the previous release staying downloadable — the last[m
[32m+[m[32m  three are always on the releases page and the site[m
[32m+[m[32m  ([W3](website.md)) links them.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Why here:* after V0 has made the number real and before the first[m
[32m+[m[32msprint on the [priorities](priorities.md) order lands — X0 and A0 are[m
[32m+[m[32mone week each, and the first release that follows them should be cut[m
[32m+[m[32mby a process, not by hand.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Done when:* a merge to `main` produces a nightly artifact within[m
[32m+[m[32mfifteen minutes; `docs/releasing.md` exists; the first sprint-driven[m
[32m+[m[32mrelease ships through the checklist with nothing skipped.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Risk:* low. The workflow exists; this adds a trigger, a check and a[m
[32m+[m[32mdocument.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### V2 — Versions and milestones (half a week)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mWhat the number means while it starts with `0`:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Minor** (`0.2` → `0.3`): a roadmap sprint landed that a user can[m
[32m+[m[32m  feel. Named after it.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Patch** (`0.2.0` → `0.2.1`): fixes only. A regression in a release[m
[32m+[m[32m  is a patch within the week, out of the train.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Nothing is removed in a minor.** Escape sequences are added, never[m
[32m+[m[32m  taken away; a config key is renamed only with the old name still[m
[32m+[m[32m  accepted for one minor.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe [priorities](priorities.md) order maps onto milestones, each a[m
[32m+[m[32mGitHub milestone with the sprint issues attached:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| Version | Name | Sprints | What a user notices |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|---|---|[m
[32m+[m[32m| 0.2 | the gallery and the corpus | X0, A0, D0 | The renderer is ours; text blends in linear light. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| 0.3 | selection | E1, D1 | You can copy. FreeType is gone. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| 0.4 | agents see themselves | A2, D2 + X2, A1 | Agent TUIs stop flickering, emoji appear, the bell reaches you. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| 0.5 | our window | D4, D5 + P0 | SDL is gone; one binary; an app anyone can install. **The first release worth telling people about.** |[m
[32m+[m[32m| 0.6 | prompts | A3, E2 | The terminal knows what each command did. |[m
[32m+[m[32m| 0.7 | tabs | A5, E5, X1 | Several agents, one window. |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**1.0 is a set of conditions, not a date:**[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Every item on the README's "Not done yet" list is done or explicitly[m
[32m+[m[32m  declined on a roadmap.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Signed and notarized; one binary; installable by cask and DMG.[m
[32m+[m[32m- The esctest known-failure list is short enough to print in the[m
[32m+[m[32m  release notes, and printed there.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Someone who is not the author has used it as their daily terminal for[m
[32m+[m[32m  a month and said so in an issue.[m
[32m+[m[32m- The config file format is declared stable.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Done when:* the milestones exist with their issues, `CHANGELOG.md`'s[m
[32m+[m[32m"Unreleased" section is grouped under the next version's name, and this[m
[32m+[m[32mtable is linked from the README.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Risk:* none, except the temptation to let the table become a schedule.[m
[32m+[m[32mIt is a map.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### V3 — Release notes people read (half a week, then per release)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe changelog section is the release body, and it has a fixed shape:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. **What you will notice** — two to five items, each one sentence,[m
[32m+[m[32m   the first with a gallery capture. Written for a user, not a[m
[32m+[m[32m   contributor.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. **Numbers** — the bench delta against the previous release and the[m
[32m+[m[32m   `--frame-stats` figures that moved, in a table. A release that moved[m
[32m+[m[32m   no number says so.[m
[32m+[m[32m3. **Fixed** — regressions and bugs, each linking the issue.[m
[32m+[m[32m4. **Known gaps** — the README's list, so nobody discovers it after[m
[32m+[m[32m   installing.[m
[32m+[m[32m5. **All changes** — the generated PR list, grouped by prefix.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEach item that closed a sprint links the sprint's record under[m
[32m+[m[32m[completed/](completed/); those records are the best writing in the[m
[32m+[m[32mrepository and the notes are where people find them.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Done when:* the next release's notes follow the shape, and the site[m
[32m+[m[32m([W3](website.md)) renders them from the same file.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Risk:* low.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### V4 — Support and security (half a week)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Supported versions:** the latest release, and nothing older, while[m
[32m+[m[32m  the version starts with `0`. `SECURITY.md` says so.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **A security fix** is a patch release within seven days of[m
[32m+[m[32m  confirmation, out of the train, with a GitHub security advisory and a[m
[32m+[m[32m  changelog line that says what was fixed once the fix is out.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Labels** that mean something: `bug`, `regression`,[m
[32m+[m[32m  `release-blocker` join the existing `perf`, `sprint`, `measured`,[m
[32m+[m[32m  `good first issue`. A `regression` is a patch-release candidate by[m
[32m+[m[32m  definition; a `release-blocker` stops the train until it is closed.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **The bug template asks for `--version` and `--doctor`**[m
[32m+[m[32m  ([P4](platform.md)) before anything else.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Done when:* `SECURITY.md` states the policy; the labels exist; the[m
[32m+[m[32mtemplate asks for the two flags.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Risk:* none.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Why this order[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **V0 first** because the repository currently describes a release that[m
[32m+[m[32m  did not happen, and every later step assumes the number is real.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **V1 before the first product sprint lands**, so it ships through a[m
[32m+[m[32m  process on the first try.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **V2 and V3 together**, since the milestone names are the release[m
[32m+[m[32m  names and the notes are written under them.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **V4 whenever a half-day is free**; it matters the day the first[m
[32m+[m[32m  outside user appears, which [P0](platform.md) is timed for.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Not on this plan[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **A beta channel.** The nightly and a week of the maintainer's use[m
[32m+[m[32m  are the beta.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Long-term support branches.** Latest only, until 1.0 and probably[m
[32m+[m[32m  after.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Automated version bumps from commit prefixes.** The number is a[m
[32m+[m[32m  decision made in the changelog, not a side effect of a merge.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Release-day marketing.** That is [website.md](website.md)'s W4, and[m
[32m+[m[32m  it is gated on a release worth marketing.[m
[1mdiff --git a/docs/roadmap/website.md b/docs/roadmap/website.md[m
[1mnew file mode 100644[m
[1mindex 0000000..c5be9cb[m
[1m--- /dev/null[m
[1m+++ b/docs/roadmap/website.md[m
[36m@@ -0,0 +1,190 @@[m
[32m+[m[32m# Website roadmap[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe marketing site, on GitHub Pages. It is the first screenshot most[m
[32m+[m[32mpeople will ever see of this terminal, so it is held to the[m
[32m+[m[32m[experience](experience.md) bar — and it is built the way the terminal[m
[32m+[m[32mis: from scratch, no framework, nothing linked that is not the[m
[32m+[m[32mplatform. Sized for one person at 8–12 focused hours a week. Sprint[m
[32m+[m[32mprefix: **W**.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mArbiter: **a fresh visitor and Lighthouse.** Someone who has never heard[m
[32m+[m[32mof the project goes from the link to a running terminal without a[m
[32m+[m[32mquestion; Lighthouse scores 100 on all four axes; and every number on[m
[32m+[m[32mthe site was generated from a file in the repository.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## The one rule for the site[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m**Nothing on the site that the repository does not already produce.**[m
[32m+[m[32mThe screenshot is a gallery capture. The numbers are `bench/baseline.txt`.[m
[32m+[m[32mThe docs are `docs/`. The release notes are `CHANGELOG.md`. The[m
[32m+[m[32mengineering stories are the sprint records. Marketing copy that can[m
[32m+[m[32mdrift from the truth is not written; a page that renders artifacts[m
[32m+[m[32mcannot drift.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Where we are[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| | Today | Where |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|---|[m
[32m+[m[32m| Site | **None.** No Pages configuration, no `gh-pages` branch, repository homepage empty | `gh api repos/…/pages` → 404 |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Screenshots | **None in the repository.** `--screenshot` exists and is unused outside `--frame-stats` runs | `render.zig` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Pitch | The README's first paragraph and the repository description | `README.md` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Docs | Fourteen files under `docs/`, readable only on GitHub | `docs/` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Numbers | `bench/baseline.txt`, `--frame-stats` output in sprint records | `bench/`, `docs/roadmap/completed/` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Changelog | `CHANGELOG.md`, Keep-a-Changelog form | — |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Name | Shared with a well-known GNOME terminal; a search for the name finds the other one | — |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Domain | None | — |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## The sprints[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### W0 — The one page (one week)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m`site/index.html` and `site/site.css`, written by hand. No build step,[m
[32m+[m[32mno JavaScript, no web font — the system monospace, which is what the[m
[32m+[m[32mterminal uses too. Deployed by an Actions workflow with[m
[32m+[m[32m`actions/deploy-pages` from `site/`, so there is no `gh-pages` branch to[m
[32m+[m[32mkeep in sync.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mOn the page, in order:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. **One real screenshot**, full width, captured with `--screenshot` at[m
[32m+[m[32m   2× — the flag exists today, so the first version ships with a real[m
[32m+[m[32m   frame, and [X0](experience.md)'s gallery replaces it with a[m
[32m+[m[32m   maintained one.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. **One sentence.** The README's: a terminal emulator for macOS,[m
[32m+[m[32m   written in Zig; the parser, the grid, the scrollback and the atlas[m
[32m+[m[32m   from scratch.[m
[32m+[m[32m3. **A download button** that links to `releases/latest` — GitHub[m
[32m+[m[32m   resolves it, no script needed — and the cask line once[m
[32m+[m[32m   [P2](platform.md) exists. Until [P1](platform.md) has signing, the[m
[32m+[m[32m   button says so in one line beneath it.[m
[32m+[m[32m4. **What is ours** — the table from [dependencies.md](dependencies.md),[m
[32m+[m[32m   which is the pitch.[m
[32m+[m[32m5. Links: docs, changelog, the repository.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDesign: the terminal's own theme, both of [X4](experience.md)'s once[m
[32m+[m[32mthey exist, following `prefers-color-scheme`. Monospace-forward,[m
[32m+[m[32mgenerous measure, one accent. It should look like a frame from the[m
[32m+[m[32mterminal, because the screenshot is one.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Why here:* the site can exist the day the screenshot can, and that day[m
[32m+[m[32mis today.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Done when:* Lighthouse 100 / 100 / 100 / 100; the page including the[m
[32m+[m[32mscreenshot is under 300 KB; it reads at 320 px wide; there is no[m
[32m+[m[32m`<script>` tag; the repository's homepage field points at it.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Risk:* low. The temptation is to add a second page; W1 is where that[m
[32m+[m[32mhappens.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### W1 — Docs and the engineering log (one week)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mA generator, `site/build.py`, beside `bench/gen_corpus.py` and with the[m
[32m+[m[32msame rule — standard library only. It renders `docs/` to `/docs/…` and[m
[32m+[m[32m`CONTRIBUTING.md` to `/contributing/`, with a Markdown subset written[m
[32m+[m[32min the script: headings, paragraphs, lists, tables, code, links,[m
[32m+[m[32memphasis. That is every construct the docs use, and the generator fails[m
[32m+[m[32mthe build on one it does not know rather than passing it through.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe sprint records under `completed/` become **the engineering log** at[m
[32m+[m[32m`/log/`, newest first, each with its date from `git log`. A 150× win, a[m
[32m+[m[32m4.3× win, and two sprints retired by their gates before a line was[m
[32m+[m[32mwritten are the best marketing the project has, and they are already[m
[32m+[m[32mwritten.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEvery internal link is checked at build time; a broken one fails the[m
[32m+[m[32mdeploy.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Why here:* after W0 exists to hang it on, and because the roadmaps and[m
[32m+[m[32mrecords are the content the site has that no competitor's does.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Done when:* every file under `docs/` has a URL; `/log/` lists every[m
[32m+[m[32mrecord; the build fails on a broken link or an unknown construct.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Risk:* low. The Markdown subset is small because the docs are[m
[32m+[m[32mdisciplined; keep both true.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### W2 — Numbers that are live (one week)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **The bench table** on the front page, rendered from[m
[32m+[m[32m  `bench/baseline.txt` at build time — corpus, MiB/s, what it is. When[m
[32m+[m[32m  the baseline changes, the site changes.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **A history**: each tagged release's baseline kept under[m
[32m+[m[32m  `bench/history/<tag>.txt`, and the front page draws one SVG line per[m
[32m+[m[32m  corpus across releases — generated by the script, no chart library,[m
[32m+[m[32m  no script tag. A number that goes down is drawn going down.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **The typography page** from the gallery, at 1× and 2×, so a visitor[m
[32m+[m[32m  can judge the rendering before installing.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **The link line** from [D5](dependencies.md) — `libc, AppKit, Metal,[m
[32m+[m[32m  QuartzCore` — as a badge, generated from `otool -L` in the release[m
[32m+[m[32m  workflow. When it is that short, say so.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Why here:* after [V1](releases.md) starts recording a baseline per[m
[32m+[m[32mrelease, so there is a history to draw.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Done when:* the numbers on the site are byte-identical to the files in[m
[32m+[m[32mthe repository at the deployed commit, checked by a test in the build.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Risk:* low.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### W3 — Releases on the site (half a week)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m`/releases/` from `CHANGELOG.md` in [V3](releases.md)'s shape, one page[m
[32m+[m[32mper version, the latest three with download links, the nightly noted[m
[32m+[m[32monce [P1](platform.md) makes it a download. An Atom feed, written by the[m
[32m+[m[32msame script — a feed is a hundred lines of XML and needs no library —[m
[32m+[m[32mcovering releases and the engineering log.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe site rebuilds on every push to `main` and on every release tag.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Done when:* a release tag produces a release page and a feed entry[m
[32m+[m[32mwithin fifteen minutes of the workflow finishing.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Risk:* low.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### W4 — Launch (one week) — **gated**[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **The name.** The site's title disambiguates —[m
[32m+[m[32m  *terminator, a terminal for macOS* — and the description says Zig in[m
[32m+[m[32m  the first line, because that is what a searcher who found the GNOME[m
[32m+[m[32m  one will not see. A domain, if one is wanted, is a custom domain on[m
[32m+[m[32m  Pages with HTTPS; until then `oddurs.github.io/terminator` is fine[m
[32m+[m[32m  and permanent.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **An Open Graph image** generated from the gallery capture, so the[m
[32m+[m[32m  link unfurls as the screenshot everywhere it is pasted.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **The README links the site** in its first paragraph.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **One post**, drafted from the engineering log — the story is[m
[32m+[m[32m  measured sprints and the two that were retired — for wherever the[m
[32m+[m[32m  maintainer wants to put it.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Gate:* not before [P1](platform.md) has signing and the[m
[32m+[m[32m[0.5 "our window"](releases.md) release has shipped. A launch that[m
[32m+[m[32msends people to a Gatekeeper dialog, or to a binary that needs[m
[32m+[m[32mHomebrew, spends the only first impression the project gets.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Done when:* a person who has never heard of the project goes from the[m
[32m+[m[32mlink to a running terminal in under two minutes with no terminal[m
[32m+[m[32mcommands; the link unfurls as a screenshot.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Risk:* low in code, high in timing. The gate is the whole sprint.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Why this order[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **W0 today**, because the screenshot flag exists and a page with one[m
[32m+[m[32m  real frame beats a page with a paragraph.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **W1 next**, because the docs and the log are the content.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **W2 after V1** has a baseline per release to draw.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **W3 with V3**, since both render the same file.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **W4 gated** on a release worth sending people to.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Not on this plan[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Analytics, cookies, a consent banner.** Nothing is collected, so[m
[32m+[m[32m  there is nothing to consent to. The site has no script tag.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **A framework, a CMS, a theme.** Two files and a script in the[m
[32m+[m[32m  standard library, like everything else here.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **A comparison table.** Other terminals are named as prior art and as[m
[32m+[m[32m  test oracles — kitty and Ghostty draw their own box glyphs, and the[m
[32m+[m[32m  docs say so — never as a column with an X in it.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **A newsletter.** The feed is the newsletter.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **A separate documentation site.** `/docs/` on this one, from the[m
[32m+[m[32m  same files.[m

[33mcommit 8e083c728c2837beee653543aebf50d9fb62906d[m
Author: Oddur Sigurdsson <oddurs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Fri Aug 28 22:21:06 2026 -0400

    docs: add product roadmaps beside the performance one (#19)
    
    Six new roadmaps under docs/roadmap/, one per product priority, plus an
    index that ranks the priorities and proposes the order of the next
    twelve sprints:
    
      priorities.md    beautiful > agentic > fast > well-rounded, and "ours"
      experience.md    typography, glyph coverage, motion, colour, chrome
      agentic.md       attention, modern-TUI protocol, OSC 133, links, tabs
      essentials.md    selection, mouse, search, reflow, config, keys
      correctness.md   conformance, Unicode, identity, robustness
      platform.md      bundle, signing, distribution, updates, diagnostics
      dependencies.md  own the GPU path, rasterizer, shaper and window
    
    Each follows the performance roadmap's form -- an audit of where the
    code is today, sprints with "why here / done when / risk", gates that
    can retire work -- and each opens by building its own arbiter (a
    gallery, a corpus, a harness) before building anything else.
    
    
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015A84EWxkDNg8oUXUHgS32P
    
    Co-authored-by: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

