[1m+++ b/docs/roadmap/agentic.md[m
[36m@@ -0,0 +1,311 @@[m
[32m+[m[32m# Agentic roadmap[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mA terminal for working with agents. The person at the keyboard is running[m
[32m+[m[32mClaude Code, Codex, aider or the next one — usually several at once, each[m
[32m+[m[32mfor minutes to hours, each occasionally needing a human. Sized for one[m
[32m+[m[32mperson at 8–12 focused hours a week. Sprint prefix: **A**.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mArbiter: **recorded agent sessions and the protocol audit table** that A0[m
[32m+[m[32mbuilds. A claim about what agents need carries a sequence from a recording[m
[32m+[m[32mor it is labelled a guess.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## What is different about an agent session[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFour things, and each one is a product decision this terminal can make[m
[32m+[m[32mthat a shell-era terminal did not have to.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m1. **It runs for a long time and then needs you.** The terminal's most[m
[32m+[m[32m   valuable moment is telling you *which* of five tabs wants an answer, and[m
[32m+[m[32m   doing it while you are in another app. Attention routing is the product.[m
[32m+[m[32m2. **It emits a great deal of structured-ish output** — tool calls, diffs,[m
[32m+[m[32m   file paths, URLs, exit codes — that you navigate rather than read[m
[32m+[m[32m   linearly. Command boundaries, clickable paths and "jump to the last[m
[32m+[m[32m   prompt" matter more than raw scrollback.[m
[32m+[m[32m3. **It is a modern TUI.** Ink, Ratatui, Bubble Tea and prompt_toolkit[m
[32m+[m[32m   reach for protocol features the VT220 never had: synchronized output,[m
[32m+[m[32m   the kitty keyboard protocol, focus events, colour queries, cursor shape,[m
[32m+[m[32m   OSC 8 links, OSC 52 clipboard. Miss one and the symptom is flicker, a[m
[32m+[m[32m   key that does nothing, or a light theme drawn on a dark background.[m
[32m+[m[32m4. **There are several of them.** One window, one PTY is the wrong shape.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Where we are[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mRead from the source, and marked as such — A0 turns this table into a[m
[32m+[m[32mmeasured one.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| Capability | Status | Where |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|---|[m
[32m+[m[32m| BEL | Sets `Terminal.bell`. **Nothing reads it.** | `terminal.zig` `execute`; no reader anywhere in `src/` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Mouse reporting (1000/1002/1003/1006) | Mode tracked as one bool; events never forwarded | `Modes.mouse`; `main.zig` `handleWheel` only |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Synchronized output (DEC 2026) | Not handled. A frame can be snapshotted between a TUI's erase and its redraw | `Renderer.snapshot` runs whenever `dirty` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Focus events (1004) | Not handled; `renderer.focused` is tracked for the cursor only | `main.zig` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| kitty keyboard protocol (`CSI > u`, `CSI = u`, `CSI ? u`) | **Mis-handled**: `'u'` restores the cursor regardless of the private marker, so a push of keyboard flags moves the cursor | `csiDispatch`, `'u'` arm |[m
[32m+[m[32m| DECSCUSR (cursor shape) | Ignored, by design, with a comment saying so | `csiDispatch` intermediates note |[m
[32m+[m[32m| OSC 0 / 2 (title) | Handled | `oscDispatch` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| OSC 7 (cwd), 8 (links), 9 / 99 / 777 (notify), 10 / 11 / 12 (colour query), 52 (clipboard), 133 (semantic prompts) | Parsed to a string, then dropped | `oscDispatch` `else => {}` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| DA1 | Answers as a VT220 | `deviceAttributes` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| DA2, XTVERSION, DECRQM | Not answered; a TUI probing for capabilities times out | — |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Bracketed paste | Handled | `Modes.bracketed_paste`, `Cmd V` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Tabs, multiple PTYs | One `App`, one `Terminal`, one `Pty` | `main.zig` |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Shift+Enter / Option+Enter | Indistinguishable from Enter | `input.zig` `.enter` |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mNothing here is a criticism of a from-scratch terminal that is a few months[m
[32m+[m[32mold. It is the list.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## The sprints[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### A0 — Agent corpus and protocol audit (one week)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mRecord real sessions: an agent given a task in this repository, captured[m
[32m+[m[32mbyte-for-byte with `script(1)` on the PTY, one file per agent CLI, plus a[m
[32m+[m[32mscripted "worst case" — an agent streaming a long diff while a build runs[m
[32m+[m[32min a second pane. Commit them under `bench/corpus/agent-*.bin` with the[m
[32m+[m[32msame seeding and byte-identity rules as the existing six.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFrom the recordings, produce two things and put them in this file:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **The audit table** — every distinct CSI, OSC, DCS and mode each agent[m
[32m+[m[32m  emits or queries, with a column for what terminator does today:[m
[32m+[m[32m  handled, ignored, mis-handled. This replaces the "where we are" table[m
[32m+[m[32m  above with a measured one.[m
[32m+[m[32m- **The shape of agent output** — bytes per write, writes per second,[m
[32m+[m[32m  cursor-up-and-redraw cycles per second, longest burst. This is what the[m
[32m+[m[32m  render path is being asked to do, and it is not what `bench/dump.sh`[m
[32m+[m[32m  does.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Why here:* every sprint below claims agents need something. This is where[m
[32m+[m[32mthe claim gets a source. It is also the cheapest sprint on any roadmap and[m
[32m+[m[32mthe only one that can retire another.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Done when:* the corpora are committed, `zig build bench` reports them[m
[32m+[m[32malongside the six, and the audit table exists with a status for every row.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m*Risk:* low. The risk is in what it finds — expect at least one row of[m
[32m+[m[32m"mis-handled" that is not in the table above.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### A1 — Attention (one week)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mMake the bell mean something. When the window is unfocused and a child[m
[32m+[m[32mrings BEL, or sends an OSC 9 / 99 / 777 notification with a message:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- post a macOS notification (a thin Cocoa shim; SDL3 has no notification[m
[32m+[m[32m  API), carrying the message if there was one and the tab title if not,[m
[32m+[m[32m  and focus the window when clicked;[m
[32m+[m[32m- badge the tab (once A5 exists) and bounce the dock icon once[m
[32m+[m[32m  (`reque